// Approved faith article, without the separate light passage.
PUBLIC_PAGES["/if-i-believe-he-is-here"] = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>If I Believe He Is Here \u00b7 Speak I Hear</title><style>\n:root{color-scheme:light;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;color:#29382f;background:#faf8f2}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0}header,main,footer{max-width:760px;margin:auto;padding:28px 24px}header{border-bottom:1px solid #d9ded4;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;align-items:center}header a{font-size:16px}a{color:#305d45;text-underline-offset:4px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,6vw,46px);font-weight:normal;line-height:1.15;margin:16px 0 24px}h2{font-size:25px;font-weight:normal}p,li{font-size:19px;line-height:1.7}.eyebrow,.notice,footer,.count{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}.eyebrow{letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5a6d5f}.notice{padding:12px 16px;background:#eeeade;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:32px}.placeholder{padding:24px;border:1px dashed #879887;background:#f1f3ec;margin:24px 0;border-radius:5px}.placeholder p{font-size:17px;margin-bottom:0}.media{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}.media .placeholder{margin:0;min-height:145px}nav.reading{margin-top:40px;border-top:1px solid #d9ded4;padding-top:24px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:24px}.next{display:inline-block;padding:13px 19px;background:#305d45;color:white;border-radius:4px;text-decoration:none;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:15px}.menu-list{padding-left:24px}.menu-list li{padding:10px 0}footer{color:#667065;border-top:1px solid #d9ded4;margin-top:32px}.count{color:#667065}a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ab753a;outline-offset:5px}@media(max-width:520px){.media{grid-template-columns:1fr}nav.reading{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}}[hidden]{display:none!important}\n</style></head><body><header><span>Speak I Hear &middot; His Love Story</span><nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"/index.html\">Main Menu</a> &middot; <a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Shared Journey</a></nav></header><main><h1>If I Believe He Is Here</h1><p><em>Our Shared Journey</em></p><p>I am not talking to myself, although I realize it may sometimes look that way.</p>\n<p>I am talking to Jesus.</p>\n<p>I may speak to Him about anything, at any time. Of course, I use wisdom about where I am and what I am doing. But underneath that ordinary consideration is a question I cannot get away from:</p>\n<p><strong>If Jesus is alive, and I believe He is alive, why would I live as though He were absent?</strong></p>\n<p>God is omnipresent. We say that readily enough.</p>\n<p>Do I believe it?</p>\n<p>Then He is right here as I write this.</p>\n<p>I do not have to summon Him. I do not have to manufacture an atmosphere that persuades Him to come near. I can turn my attention toward the One who is already present.</p>\n<p>\u201cLord, how do I explain this?\u201d</p>\n<p>Even that question can become part of our conversation.</p>\n<p>Could He be helping me find the words? I believe He can. That does not mean everything I write is something God has said. My understanding needs correction, and my thoughts must be examined in the light of His Word.</p>\n<p>But neither do I want to become so reluctant to acknowledge His involvement that I behave as though He has nothing to do with my ordinary life.</p>\n<p>He is alive.</p>\n<p>I believe Him.</p>\n<p>I want my way of living to reflect that.</p>\n<p>To someone watching from the outside, I may seem a mess. Here is a man speaking to Someone they cannot see, loving Someone they have never met, and arranging his life around a relationship they may not understand.</p>\n<p>\u201cTake him away to the funny farm!\u201d</p>\n<p>Well, let me explain what I mean.</p>\n<p>I am not claiming that my natural eyes have begun seeing a figure standing beside me. These ordinary orbs of sight still do what they have always done. They report the physical world around me.</p>\n<p><strong>But physical sight is not the measure of everything that is real.</strong></p>\n<p>In my relationship with Christ, I have found an abiding love. As I have come to know His love, my confidence in Him has grown.</p>\n<p>I have learned that I can bring Him things I once thought I had to carry alone. I can speak honestly. I can ask questions. I can acknowledge that I do not understand.</p>\n<p>I can also be quiet and give my attention to Him.</p>\n<p>Over time, that relationship changes what I notice.</p>\n<p>I begin to recognize occasions for gratitude where I once saw only ordinary circumstances. I become more attentive to the needs of another person. His Word comes to bear on a decision, an attitude, or a response I might previously have overlooked.</p>\n<p>I find myself recognizing His care in places where I had not thought to look.</p>\n<p>When I say that I see Him everywhere, that is what I am describing.</p>\n<p>I do not mean that everything around me is God. I mean that nothing in my life takes place beyond His presence, and that His creation continually gives me reasons to remember Him.</p>\n<p>The familiar becomes an invitation to acknowledge the One I love.</p>\n<p>\u201cLord, thank You.\u201d</p>\n<p>\u201cHelp me understand.\u201d</p>\n<p>\u201cWhat would please You here?\u201d</p>\n<p>Those are ordinary words. Yet they express a remarkable reality: I am living my natural life in fellowship with the Living God.</p>\n<p>That awareness has developed over time. I am still learning.</p>\n<p>What I am calling spiritual eyesight has very little to do with these orbs of sight and a great deal to do with the perspective from which I understand my life.</p>\n<p>If I regard my physical surroundings as the whole of reality, speaking to Jesus throughout the day may seem peculiar.</p>\n<p>If I understand that I already belong to His eternal Kingdom, acknowledging Him becomes perfectly natural.</p>\n<p>Why would I leave Him out of the conversation?</p>\n<p>Why would I speak of His presence in church, then spend the rest of the week acting as though He were somewhere else?</p>\n<p>Why would I profess that He loves me, yet hesitate to bring Him the ordinary things on my heart?</p>\n<p><strong>Knowing His love has increased my faith.</strong></p>\n<p>I am growing more confident in the One I am coming to know.</p>\n<p>That confidence allows me to turn toward Him in the middle of an unfinished day, with unfinished work and an unfinished understanding of nearly everything.</p>\n<p>I do not have to make an impressive speech.</p>\n<p>\u201cJesus, I love You.\u201d</p>\n<p>He is here when I say it.</p>\n<p>He was here before I remembered to say it.</p>\n<p>And when I return to the ordinary task before me, I have no reason to suppose our fellowship has ended.</p>\n<p>Perhaps that is where faith begins to change the texture of a day: when what I say I believe becomes part of how I actually live.</p>\n<p>Jesus is alive.</p>\n<p>God is present.</p>\n<p>I am loved.</p>\n<p>Now, how will I live the next few minutes in the light of that?</p>\n<p>That has a great deal to do with your eternal perspective.</p>\n<p>Speaking of that\u2026</p>\n<p>Perhaps it is time to consider <a href=\"https://speakihear.org/changing-your-perspective\">changing your perspective</a>.</p><nav class=\"reading\" aria-label=\"Reading navigation\"><a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Shared Journey</a><a href=\"/index.html\">Main Menu</a></nav></main></body></html>";
