PUBLIC_PAGES["/changing-your-perspective"] = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>Changing Your Perspective \u00b7 Speak I Hear</title><style>\n:root{color-scheme:light;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;color:#29382f;background:#faf8f2}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0}header,main,footer{max-width:760px;margin:auto;padding:28px 24px}header{border-bottom:1px solid #d9ded4;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;align-items:center}header a{font-size:16px}a{color:#305d45;text-underline-offset:4px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,6vw,46px);font-weight:normal;line-height:1.15;margin:16px 0 24px}h2{font-size:25px;font-weight:normal}p,li{font-size:19px;line-height:1.7}.eyebrow,.notice,footer,.count{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}.eyebrow{letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5a6d5f}.notice{padding:12px 16px;background:#eeeade;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:32px}.placeholder{padding:24px;border:1px dashed #879887;background:#f1f3ec;margin:24px 0;border-radius:5px}.placeholder p{font-size:17px;margin-bottom:0}.media{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}.media .placeholder{margin:0;min-height:145px}nav.reading{margin-top:40px;border-top:1px solid #d9ded4;padding-top:24px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:24px}.next{display:inline-block;padding:13px 19px;background:#305d45;color:white;border-radius:4px;text-decoration:none;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:15px}.menu-list{padding-left:24px}.menu-list li{padding:10px 0}footer{color:#667065;border-top:1px solid #d9ded4;margin-top:32px}.count{color:#667065}a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ab753a;outline-offset:5px}@media(max-width:520px){.media{grid-template-columns:1fr}nav.reading{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}}[hidden]{display:none!important}\n</style></head><body><header><span>Speak I Hear &middot; His Love Story</span><nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"/index.html\">Main Menu</a> &middot; <a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Shared Journey</a></nav></header><main><h1>Changing Your Perspective</h1><p><em>Our Shared Journey</em></p><p><strong>I am a spiritual man who just happens to have a natural body.</strong></p>\n<p>That is my perspective. I would like to invite you to consider making it yours.</p>\n<p>Why would you want to do that?</p>\n<p>Well, let me explain.</p>\n<p>When I awaken in the morning, it is perfectly natural for me to say, \u201cGod, I love You.\u201d</p>\n<p>Perhaps that sounds a little sappy. After all, isn&#x27;t the first thing on your mind when you awaken something more practical? Like needing to go to the bathroom?</p>\n<p>Not necessarily.</p>\n<p>You see, from the moment we enter this world, nearly everything we learn concerns our physical existence. We learn to breathe, eat, walk, speak, and satisfy the demands of this remarkable body. We discover hunger, pain, pleasure, fear, and desire. Our senses introduce us to a world that seems to be everything there is.</p>\n<p>For much of our lives, we accept that perspective without question.</p>\n<p>Yet something extraordinary has happened to those of us who belong to Christ.</p>\n<p>We have become partakers of a Kingdom that is eternal. We have been given life that does not begin when this body dies. <strong>Eternal life is already ours.</strong></p>\n<p>Jesus said, \u201cAnd this is eternal life, that they know you, the only true God, and Jesus Christ whom you have sent.\u201d \u2014 John 17:3 (ESV)</p>\n<p>Notice that He describes eternal life in terms of knowing Him.</p>\n<p>That changes the way I think about everything.</p>\n<p>If I already possess eternal life, why would I continue living as though my natural circumstances define my existence? Why would I allow the temporary things I can see to dominate my thoughts while paying so little attention to the eternal reality in which I already participate?</p>\n<p>Paul wrote:</p>\n<p>\u201cFor the things which are seen are temporal; but the things which are not seen are eternal.\u201d \u2014 2 Corinthians 4:18 (KJV)</p>\n<p>Think about that for a moment.</p>\n<p>The eternal isn&#x27;t simply something waiting for me after death. I already belong to it. I am already a citizen of God&#x27;s Kingdom, even while I continue living here in this natural body.</p>\n<p>My physical senses report what is happening around me. They tell me when I am hungry, tired, uncomfortable, or in pain. They alert me to responsibilities that require attention. There is nothing wrong with any of that. God gave me this wonderful body, and I am grateful for it.</p>\n<p>But my senses cannot tell me everything about the life I am living.</p>\n<p>They cannot measure communion with God. They cannot reveal the full extent of His purposes, or explain the spiritual reality in which I have already been invited to participate.</p>\n<p>For that, I must learn to give my attention to Him.</p>\n<p>I believe God created mankind originally embodied, able to live in communion with Him at the intersection of the physical and spiritual realms. Our present mortal condition does not resemble that original existence in its fullness. Yet in Christ I see what humanity is being restored to become.</p>\n<p>And while I look forward to being clothed with the resurrected life He now possesses, I do not have to wait until then to begin living in fellowship with Him.</p>\n<p><strong>I can know Him now.</strong></p>\n<p>That brings me to something very practical.</p>\n<p>What occupies your thoughts when you awaken?</p>\n<p>For many people, the demands of the day begin almost immediately. We think about appointments, responsibilities, difficulties, unfinished work, and the countless things requiring our attention.</p>\n<p>I have those things too.</p>\n<p>But I have discovered that I can begin somewhere else.</p>\n<p>\u201cGod, I love You.\u201d</p>\n<p>Those words are not a ritual. They are the natural expression of a relationship that continues whether I am awake or asleep, busy or resting, joyful or troubled.</p>\n<p>I do not need to arrange an appointment to speak with Him. I do not need to enter a particular building or wait for some extraordinary spiritual occasion.</p>\n<p>He is already present.</p>\n<p>The more I become accustomed to acknowledging that relationship, the more naturally it becomes part of everything I do.</p>\n<p>I can speak with Him while working, driving, walking, or sitting quietly. I can bring Him my questions, my gratitude, my confusion, and even those moments when I have no idea what to say.</p>\n<p>I can learn what pleases Him. I can become more familiar with His Word, recognize where my thinking differs from His, and allow Him to change my understanding.</p>\n<p>This is not a technique for manufacturing spiritual experiences.</p>\n<p><strong>It is learning to live in a relationship that already exists.</strong></p>\n<p>Consider how differently we might approach our lives if we genuinely understood that.</p>\n<p>Our circumstances would still matter, but they would no longer be the whole story. Our bodies would still require care, our responsibilities would still need attention, and difficulties would not simply disappear.</p>\n<p>Yet through all of it, we could remain conscious that we belong to an eternal Kingdom and that our lives are being shaped by its King.</p>\n<p>I want to become like Him.</p>\n<p>Not merely to know more facts about Jesus, or become more accomplished at religious activities, but to know Him so intimately that His character increasingly becomes evident in the way I think, speak, respond, and live.</p>\n<p>That is what I am seeking.</p>\n<p>I am a spiritual man who just happens to have a natural body.</p>\n<p>I am already living in eternity, although I have not yet experienced everything God has promised.</p>\n<p>So here is my invitation to you.</p>\n<p><strong>Change your perspective.</strong></p>\n<p>You have spent much of your life looking at eternity through the narrow window of your natural existence.</p>\n<p>What might happen if you began looking at your natural existence from the perspective of eternity?</p>\n<p>What if, instead of treating your relationship with God as one part of your life, you began recognizing that every part of your life takes place within that relationship?</p>\n<p>Perhaps tomorrow morning, before the ordinary demands of the day begin, you might simply say:</p>\n<p>\u201cGod, I love You.\u201d</p>\n<p>Then spend the rest of the day learning what it means to live as someone who already belongs to Him.</p><section aria-labelledby=\"scripture-references\"><h2 id=\"scripture-references\">Scripture references</h2><p>Passages for reading and reflection alongside this writing.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John%2017%3A3&amp;version=KJV\">John 17:3</a> \u2014 Eternal life described as knowing God and Jesus Christ.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John%205%3A24&amp;version=KJV\">John 5:24</a> \u2014 The believer has eternal life and has passed from death to life.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=2%20Corinthians%204%3A16-18&amp;version=KJV\">2 Corinthians 4:16\u201318</a> \u2014 Giving attention to the eternal while the outward person ages.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Colossians%201%3A12-14&amp;version=KJV\">Colossians 1:12\u201314</a> \u2014 Belonging to the Kingdom of God\u2019s Son.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Colossians%203%3A1-4&amp;version=KJV\">Colossians 3:1\u20134</a> \u2014 Setting our minds on things above; our life hidden with Christ.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Philippians%203%3A20-21&amp;version=KJV\">Philippians 3:20\u201321</a> \u2014 Citizenship in heaven and the promised transformation of our bodies.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=2%20Corinthians%205%3A1-9&amp;version=KJV\">2 Corinthians 5:1\u20139</a> \u2014 Longing to be clothed with heavenly life and seeking to please the Lord.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis%202%3A7%3B%203%3A8-19&amp;version=KJV\">Genesis 2:7; 3:8\u201319</a> \u2014 Humanity\u2019s creation, relationship with God, and the consequences of the fall.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Romans%208%3A29&amp;version=KJV\">Romans 8:29</a> \u2014 God\u2019s purpose that His people be conformed to the image of His Son.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Romans%2012%3A1-2&amp;version=KJV\">Romans 12:1\u20132</a> \u2014 Offering our lives to God and being transformed through renewed minds.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1%20Thessalonians%205%3A16-18&amp;version=KJV\">1 Thessalonians 5:16\u201318</a> \u2014 Prayer and gratitude throughout daily life.</li></ul></section><nav class=\"reading\" aria-label=\"Reading navigation\"><a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Shared Journey</a><a href=\"/index.html\">Main Menu</a><a class=\"next\" href=\"/if-i-believe-he-is-here\">Next: If I Believe He Is Here \u2192</a></nav></main></body></html>";

PUBLIC_PAGES["/if-i-believe-he-is-here"] = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>If I Believe He Is Here \u00b7 Speak I Hear</title><style>\n:root{color-scheme:light;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;color:#29382f;background:#faf8f2}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0}header,main,footer{max-width:760px;margin:auto;padding:28px 24px}header{border-bottom:1px solid #d9ded4;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;align-items:center}header a{font-size:16px}a{color:#305d45;text-underline-offset:4px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,6vw,46px);font-weight:normal;line-height:1.15;margin:16px 0 24px}h2{font-size:25px;font-weight:normal}p,li{font-size:19px;line-height:1.7}.eyebrow,.notice,footer,.count{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}.eyebrow{letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5a6d5f}.notice{padding:12px 16px;background:#eeeade;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:32px}.placeholder{padding:24px;border:1px dashed #879887;background:#f1f3ec;margin:24px 0;border-radius:5px}.placeholder p{font-size:17px;margin-bottom:0}.media{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}.media .placeholder{margin:0;min-height:145px}nav.reading{margin-top:40px;border-top:1px solid #d9ded4;padding-top:24px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:24px}.next{display:inline-block;padding:13px 19px;background:#305d45;color:white;border-radius:4px;text-decoration:none;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:15px}.menu-list{padding-left:24px}.menu-list li{padding:10px 0}footer{color:#667065;border-top:1px solid #d9ded4;margin-top:32px}.count{color:#667065}a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ab753a;outline-offset:5px}@media(max-width:520px){.media{grid-template-columns:1fr}nav.reading{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}}[hidden]{display:none!important}\n</style></head><body><header><span>Speak I Hear &middot; His Love Story</span><nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"/index.html\">Main Menu</a> &middot; <a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Shared Journey</a></nav></header><main><h1>If I Believe He Is Here</h1><p><em>Our Shared Journey</em></p><p>I am not talking to myself, although I realize it may sometimes look that way.</p>\n<p>I am talking to Jesus.</p>\n<p>I may speak to Him about anything, at any time. Of course, I use wisdom about where I am and what I am doing. But underneath that ordinary consideration is a question I cannot get away from:</p>\n<p><strong>If Jesus is alive, and I believe He is alive, why would I live as though He were absent?</strong></p>\n<p>God is omnipresent. We say that readily enough.</p>\n<p>Do I believe it?</p>\n<p>Then He is right here as I write this.</p>\n<p>I do not have to summon Him. I do not have to manufacture an atmosphere that persuades Him to come near. I can turn my attention toward the One who is already present.</p>\n<p>\u201cLord, how do I explain this?\u201d</p>\n<p>Even that question can become part of our conversation.</p>\n<p>Could He be helping me find the words? I believe He can. That does not mean everything I write is something God has said. My understanding needs correction, and my thoughts must be examined in the light of His Word.</p>\n<p>But neither do I want to become so reluctant to acknowledge His involvement that I behave as though He has nothing to do with my ordinary life.</p>\n<p>He is alive.</p>\n<p>I believe Him.</p>\n<p>I want my way of living to reflect that.</p>\n<p>To someone watching from the outside, I may seem a mess. Here is a man speaking to Someone they cannot see, loving Someone they have never met, and arranging his life around a relationship they may not understand.</p>\n<p>\u201cTake him away to the funny farm!\u201d</p>\n<p>Well, let me explain what I mean.</p>\n<p>I am not claiming that my natural eyes have begun seeing a figure standing beside me. These ordinary orbs of sight still do what they have always done. They report the physical world around me.</p>\n<p><strong>But physical sight is not the measure of everything that is real.</strong></p>\n<p>In my relationship with Christ, I have found an abiding love. As I have come to know His love, my confidence in Him has grown.</p>\n<p>I have learned that I can bring Him things I once thought I had to carry alone. I can speak honestly. I can ask questions. I can acknowledge that I do not understand.</p>\n<p>I can also be quiet and give my attention to Him.</p>\n<p>Over time, that relationship changes what I notice.</p>\n<p>I begin to recognize occasions for gratitude where I once saw only ordinary circumstances. I become more attentive to the needs of another person. His Word comes to bear on a decision, an attitude, or a response I might previously have overlooked.</p>\n<p>I find myself recognizing His care in places where I had not thought to look.</p>\n<p>When I say that I see Him everywhere, that is what I am describing.</p>\n<p>I do not mean that everything around me is God. I mean that nothing in my life takes place beyond His presence, and that His creation continually gives me reasons to remember Him.</p>\n<p>The familiar becomes an invitation to acknowledge the One I love.</p>\n<p>\u201cLord, thank You.\u201d</p>\n<p>\u201cHelp me understand.\u201d</p>\n<p>\u201cWhat would please You here?\u201d</p>\n<p>Those are ordinary words. Yet they express a remarkable reality: I am living my natural life in fellowship with the Living God.</p>\n<p>That awareness has developed over time. I am still learning.</p>\n<p>What I am calling spiritual eyesight has very little to do with these orbs of sight and a great deal to do with the perspective from which I understand my life.</p>\n<p>If I regard my physical surroundings as the whole of reality, speaking to Jesus throughout the day may seem peculiar.</p>\n<p>If I understand that I already belong to His eternal Kingdom, acknowledging Him becomes perfectly natural.</p>\n<p>Why would I leave Him out of the conversation?</p>\n<p>Why would I speak of His presence in church, then spend the rest of the week acting as though He were somewhere else?</p>\n<p>Why would I profess that He loves me, yet hesitate to bring Him the ordinary things on my heart?</p>\n<p><strong>Knowing His love has increased my faith.</strong></p>\n<p>I am growing more confident in the One I am coming to know.</p>\n<p>That confidence allows me to turn toward Him in the middle of an unfinished day, with unfinished work and an unfinished understanding of nearly everything.</p>\n<p>I do not have to make an impressive speech.</p>\n<p>\u201cJesus, I love You.\u201d</p>\n<p>He is here when I say it.</p>\n<p>He was here before I remembered to say it.</p>\n<p>And when I return to the ordinary task before me, I have no reason to suppose our fellowship has ended.</p>\n<p>Perhaps that is where faith begins to change the texture of a day: when what I say I believe becomes part of how I actually live.</p>\n<p>Jesus is alive.</p>\n<p>God is present.</p>\n<p>I am loved.</p>\n<p>Now, how will I live the next few minutes in the light of that?</p>\n<p>That has a great deal to do with your eternal perspective.</p>\n<p>Speaking of that\u2026</p>\n<p>Perhaps it is time to consider <a href=\"https://speakihear.org/changing-your-perspective\">changing your perspective</a>.</p><section aria-labelledby=\"scripture-references\"><h2 id=\"scripture-references\">Scripture references</h2><p>Passages for reading and reflection alongside this writing.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Revelation%201%3A17-18&amp;version=KJV\">Revelation 1:17\u201318</a> \u2014 Jesus is alive forevermore.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm%20139%3A1-12&amp;version=KJV\">Psalm 139:1\u201312</a> \u2014 God knows us and is present wherever we go.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John%2014%3A16-23&amp;version=KJV\">John 14:16\u201323</a> \u2014 The promised presence of the Spirit and fellowship with the Father and Son.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Hebrews%2013%3A5-6&amp;version=KJV\">Hebrews 13:5\u20136</a> \u2014 God\u2019s promise never to leave or forsake His people.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1%20Thessalonians%205%3A16-18&amp;version=KJV\">1 Thessalonians 5:16\u201318</a> \u2014 Continual prayer, rejoicing, and thanksgiving.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Philippians%204%3A6-7&amp;version=KJV\">Philippians 4:6\u20137</a> \u2014 Bringing our concerns to God in prayer with thanksgiving.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=2%20Corinthians%205%3A7&amp;version=KJV\">2 Corinthians 5:7</a> \u2014 Walking by faith rather than sight.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1%20John%204%3A16-19&amp;version=KJV\">1 John 4:16\u201319</a> \u2014 Knowing and believing God\u2019s love, and responding in love.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm%2019%3A1-4&amp;version=KJV\">Psalm 19:1\u20134</a> \u2014 Creation declaring the glory of God.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=2%20Timothy%203%3A16-17&amp;version=KJV\">2 Timothy 3:16\u201317</a> \u2014 Scripture teaching, correcting, and equipping us.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Colossians%203%3A17&amp;version=KJV\">Colossians 3:17</a> \u2014 Doing everything in the name of Jesus with thanksgiving.</li></ul></section><nav class=\"reading\" aria-label=\"Reading navigation\"><a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Shared Journey</a><a href=\"/index.html\">Main Menu</a><a class=\"next\" href=\"/the-wisdom-of-dawn-key\">Next: The Wisdom of Dawn Key \u2192</a></nav></main></body></html>";
// Heartbeat artwork and the invitation reflection.
PUBLIC_PAGES["/index.html"] = "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>The Heartbeat of Heaven \u00b7 The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Christ-centered writings exploring the love of God: The Greatest Love Story Ever Told, The Invitation, and The Heartbeat of Heaven.\">\n<style>\n:root{--paper:#f7f3ec;--ink:#302b28;--muted:#6b6258;--gold:#85613a;--line:#dcd2c4}*{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-behavior:smooth;scroll-padding-top:24px}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;line-height:1.7}a{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:5px}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--gold);outline-offset:6px}.wrap{width:min(1120px,90%);margin:auto}header{padding:24px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}header .wrap{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:22px;align-items:center}.brand{font-size:18px;text-decoration:none}nav{display:flex;gap:28px;font:13px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}nav a{text-decoration:none}nav a:hover{text-decoration:underline}.eyebrow{font:11px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold)}.intro{text-align:center;padding:57px 0 32px}h1,h2{font-weight:400;line-height:1.12;margin:16px 0}h1{font-size:clamp(39px,5.5vw,66px);max-width:790px;margin:15px auto 22px;letter-spacing:-.035em}.lede{max-width:620px;margin:0 auto;color:var(--muted);font-size:18px}.hero{margin:10px 0 0}.hero img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.hero figcaption{font:11px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;text-align:right;color:var(--muted);padding-top:9px}blockquote{margin:0;text-align:center;padding:48px 15px 55px;font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,31px);line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}blockquote span{display:block}.writing{padding:65px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.45fr;gap:80px}.writing h2{font-size:42px;letter-spacing:-.025em}.writing p{margin:0 0 20px;font-size:18px;color:var(--muted)}.number{font:12px system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:18px}.small{font:12px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--muted)}details{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:14px}summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--gold);font-size:16px}details p{padding-top:18px}.heartbeat{border-block:1px solid var(--line);display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:65px;align-items:center;padding:65px 0}.heartbeat img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.heartbeat h2{font-size:42px;letter-spacing:-.025em}.heartbeat p{font-size:18px;color:var(--muted)}.closing{text-align:center;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:45px 20px}.closing p{margin:8px auto;max-width:620px}.blessing{font-style:italic;font-size:25px}footer{background:#eae3d8;padding:20px;text-align:center;font:11px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:650px){header .wrap{flex-direction:column;gap:12px}nav{gap:20px}.intro{padding-top:36px}.writing,.heartbeat{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:23px;padding:40px 0}.writing h2,.heartbeat h2{font-size:35px}.heartbeat img{max-width:440px;margin:auto}blockquote{padding:32px 0}.hero figcaption{text-align:left}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}}\n.begin{display:inline-block;margin:24px 0 8px;padding:12px 24px;background:#76522e;color:white;border-radius:3px;font:15px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;text-decoration:none}.chapter-list{list-style:none;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px}.chapter-list li{padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px}.chapter-list .available{grid-column:1/-1;background:#eee6d9}.chapter-list span{display:block;font:14px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--muted);margin-top:5px}#story-thread{padding:40px 0}#story-thread h2{font-size:38px}@media(max-width:650px){.chapter-list{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:360px){.chapter-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}}.story-title{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,58px);max-width:800px;margin:15px auto 22px}.heartbeat h1{margin:14px 0 22px}#scripture{padding:40px 0 50px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}#scripture h2{font-size:38px}#scripture p{font-size:18px;color:var(--muted)}nav{flex-wrap:wrap}\n.invitation{padding:72px 0 34px}.invitation-copy{max-width:690px;margin:auto;font-size:20px;color:var(--muted)}.invitation-copy p{margin:0 0 22px}.invitation-copy .personal{font-size:25px;color:var(--ink);margin:30px auto 0;max-width:630px}.hero{margin:0 0 54px}.heartbeat{border-top:0}.story{padding:70px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:center}.story h2{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,52px);max-width:690px;margin:16px auto}.story>p{color:var(--muted);font-size:18px}.actions{display:flex;gap:24px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}.actions .begin{margin:12px 0}.story .actions{justify-content:center}.download{font:15px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}.format{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.chapter-directory{text-align:left;margin-top:30px}.chapter-directory #story-thread{padding:20px 0 0}#scripture{text-align:center;border-top:0;padding:60px 0}.personal-note{padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.personal-note .writing{border:0}.personal-note blockquote{border:0}.heartbeat h2{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,52px)}@media(max-width:650px){.invitation{padding-top:42px}.invitation-copy{font-size:18px}.invitation-copy .personal{font-size:23px}.hero{margin-bottom:20px}.story{padding:42px 0}.actions{gap:18px}}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body id=\"top\">\n<header><div class=\"wrap\"><a class=\"brand\" href=\"#top\">The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</a><nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"#heartbeat\">Heartbeat of Heaven</a><a href=\"#love-story\">The Love Story</a><a href=\"#scripture\">Scripture</a><a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Shared Journey</a></nav></div></header>\n<main class=\"wrap\"><p class=\"revision\" data-revision=\"1\" style=\"font:12px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#6b6258\">Revision 1 \u00b7 November 6, 2026</p>\n<section class=\"intro invitation\" aria-labelledby=\"invitation-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">You are welcome here</div><h1 id=\"invitation-title\">An invitation into<br>overwhelming Love</h1><div class=\"invitation-copy\"><p>There is a love so deep, so wide, and so overwhelming that a lifetime can only begin to discover it\u2014the love of God, revealed in Jesus Christ.</p><p>These writings are an invitation to pause, to wonder, and to discover the heart behind that love. Take your time. Come with your questions, your hopes, and your story.</p><p class=\"personal\">It doesn't matter who you are. If you're reading this, this love is for you.</p></div></section>\n<p class=\"reflection-link\" style=\"text-align:center;margin:0 auto 34px;font-style:italic\"><a href=\"/i-would-and-ye-would-not\">I would \u2026 and ye would not</a></p>\n<figure class=\"hero\"><img src=\"/assets/heartbeat-of-heaven-v2.jpg\" width=\"1672\" height=\"941\" alt=\"A luminous golden heartbeat forms a cross amid clouds and a deep blue, star-filled sky.\"><figcaption>The Heartbeat of Heaven</figcaption></figure>\n<section class=\"heartbeat\" id=\"heartbeat\" aria-labelledby=\"heartbeat-title\"><img src=\"/assets/heartbeat-of-heaven-v2.jpg\" width=\"1672\" height=\"941\" alt=\"A golden heartbeat forming a luminous cross.\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">A place to begin \u00b7 A short book</div><h2 id=\"heartbeat-title\">The Heartbeat<br>of Heaven</h2><p>A heartbeat. A Cross. An invitation to consider the heart of God, revealed in Christ.</p><div class=\"actions\"><a class=\"begin\" href=\"writings/heartbeat-of-heaven.html\">Read Online</a><a class=\"download\" href=\"writings/heartbeat-of-heaven-rev-r-a.pdf\" download>Download <span class=\"format\">PDF</span></a></div></div></section>\n<section class=\"story\" id=\"love-story\" aria-labelledby=\"story-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">The unfolding story</div><h2 id=\"story-title\">The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</h2><p>From Separation to Reconciliation</p><div class=\"actions\"><a class=\"begin\" href=\"writings/chapter-0.html\">Read Online</a><a class=\"download\" href=\"writings/the-greatest-love-story-current-chapters.zip\" download>Download <span class=\"format\">ZIP \u00b7 Current writings</span></a></div><p class=\"small\">The download contains all current readings in story order.</p><details class=\"chapter-directory\"><summary>Follow the story</summary><span id=\"chapters\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><section id=\"story-thread\" aria-labelledby=\"chapters-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Follow the family through time</div><h2 id=\"chapters-title\">One love story through the generations</h2><ul class=\"chapter-list\"><li class=\"available\"><a href=\"writings/chapter-0.html\">From Separation to Reconciliation</a><span>Begin reading</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/chapter-1.html\">Before the Beginning</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/chapter-2.html\">The First Home</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/chapter-3.html\">Love\u2019s Promise Within a Family</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/chapter-4.html\">Love Carried from Household to Household</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/love-comes-again-to-bethlehem.html\">Love Comes Again to Bethlehem</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/about-his-fathers-business.html\">About His Father\u2019s Business</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/love-goes-to-bring-them-home.html\">Love Goes to Bring Them Home</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/the-love-that-carries-him.html\">The Love That Carries Him</a><span>Continue the story</span></li></ul></section></details><details class=\"personal-note\" id=\"word-of-gratitude\"><summary>A Word of Gratitude</summary><div style=\"max-width:690px;margin:24px auto;text-align:left\"><p class=\"small\">An author\u2019s note</p><p>The work of Dr. Michael S. Heiser helped set me on this journey. His writing opened questions I had not known to ask and encouraged me to look again at the larger story unfolding through Scripture, particularly its glimpses of the unseen realm.</p><p>I regard his work as a blessing from the Lord, and I am grateful for what it stirred in me. As we follow this love story into places his scholarship helped me notice, I want to acknowledge that debt with affection and thanks.</p></div></details></section>\n<section id=\"scripture\" aria-labelledby=\"scripture-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Read and explore</div><h2 id=\"scripture-title\">Explore Scripture</h2><p>Open the Bible and explore the story for yourself.</p><p><a class=\"begin\" href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Visit Bible Gateway \u2197</a></p><p><a href=\"writings/scripture-references.html\">Scripture references from these writings \u2192</a></p></section>\n<details class=\"personal-note\"><summary>Why I\u2019m sharing this</summary><section class=\"writing\" id=\"why-im-sharing\" aria-labelledby=\"why-title\"><div><h2 id=\"why-title\">Why I\u2019m sharing this</h2></div><div><p>I hadn\u2019t planned to make this website. It began quite suddenly, with a desire to share something I have found to be true: God loves us, and His love is worth looking into.</p><p>These writings grow out of my own experience, questions, and reading of the Bible. I\u2019m still learning. I don\u2019t have every answer, but I have found something here that has given me hope, and I want to share it.</p><p>I\u2019m not selling anything or asking anything from you. My hope is simply that something you read here will help you\u2014whether it gives you encouragement, helps you consider a question, or leads you to open the Bible for yourself.</p><p>You\u2019re welcome to take your time.</p></div></section><blockquote>The universe exists because of Love.<span>Love does not exist because of the universe.</span></blockquote></details>\n<section id=\"testimonies\" class=\"closing\" aria-labelledby=\"testimonies-title\"><h2 id=\"testimonies-title\">Our Shared Journey</h2><p>People, places, and memories from our life together in God\u2019s family.</p><p><a href=\"/testimonies\">Visit Our Shared Journey \u2192</a></p></section><section class=\"closing\" aria-label=\"Welcome\"><p class=\"blessing\">May God bless you.</p><p>Welcome. Take your time, and may these writings turn your attention toward Christ.</p></section>\n</main>\n<footer>The Greatest Love Story Ever Told \u00b7 Christ-centered writings<p><a href=\"mailto:sam.thomas@speakihear.org\">Contact: sam.thomas@speakihear.org</a></p><p>Your thoughts and questions are welcome. Personal replies may take time.</p></footer>\n</body></html>\n";
PUBLIC_PAGES["/i-would-and-ye-would-not"] = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>I Would \u2026 and Ye Would Not \u00b7 Our Shared Journey</title><style>\n:root{color-scheme:light;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;color:#29382f;background:#faf8f2}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0}header,main,footer{max-width:760px;margin:auto;padding:28px 24px}header{border-bottom:1px solid #d9ded4;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;align-items:center}header a{font-size:16px}a{color:#305d45;text-underline-offset:4px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,6vw,46px);font-weight:normal;line-height:1.15;margin:16px 0 24px}h2{font-size:25px;font-weight:normal}p,li{font-size:19px;line-height:1.7}.eyebrow,.notice,footer,.count{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}.eyebrow{letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5a6d5f}.notice{padding:12px 16px;background:#eeeade;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:32px}.placeholder{padding:24px;border:1px dashed #879887;background:#f1f3ec;margin:24px 0;border-radius:5px}.placeholder p{font-size:17px;margin-bottom:0}.media{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}.media .placeholder{margin:0;min-height:145px}nav.reading{margin-top:40px;border-top:1px solid #d9ded4;padding-top:24px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:24px}.next{display:inline-block;padding:13px 19px;background:#305d45;color:white;border-radius:4px;text-decoration:none;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:15px}.menu-list{padding-left:24px}.menu-list li{padding:10px 0}footer{color:#667065;border-top:1px solid #d9ded4;margin-top:32px}.count{color:#667065}a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ab753a;outline-offset:5px}@media(max-width:520px){.media{grid-template-columns:1fr}nav.reading{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}}[hidden]{display:none!important}\n</style></head><body><header><span>Speak I Hear &middot; His Love Story</span><nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"/index.html\">Main Menu</a> &middot; <a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Shared Journey</a></nav></header><main><nav class=\"reading\" aria-label=\"Return navigation\"><a href=\"/index.html#invitation-title\">Return to the Invitation</a><a href=\"/testimonies#helps\">Writings for the Journey</a></nav><h1>I Would \u2026 and Ye Would Not</h1><p><em>What will we do with the love God offers?</em></p><p>Jesus looked upon Jerusalem and spoke of how often He would have gathered her children as a hen gathers her chicks beneath her wings. Then came the words:</p><p><strong>\u201cAnd ye would not.\u201d \u2014 Matthew 23:37</strong></p><p>There is something in that sentence that makes me stop. He wanted to gather them. They would not come.</p><p>We understand something of rejected love in human relationships. We know what it means to open our hearts to someone who turns away. We cannot assume that an eternal, omnipotent God experiences everything exactly as we do. But here Jesus lets us hear His lament. His invitation was real, and so was their refusal.</p><p>The God whose love we have been describing knows the answer we are giving Him. He hears our words and sees the life beneath them: what interests us, what we pursue, what we conceal, and where we welcome His involvement. He knows the thoughts we would never say aloud.</p><p>If He is real, then He is real here, too\u2014in this decision, this desire, this ordinary moment when I choose whether to give Him my attention.</p><p>That sobers me.</p><p>Balaam heard God speak. He received correction and delivered messages God gave him. Yet Scripture remembers his greed and his counsel that led others into sin. Centuries later, the risen Jesus brought Balaam\u2019s name into a warning to His church. An encounter with God had not settled how Balaam would answer Him.</p><p>What am I doing with what God has made known to me?</p><p>I am not asking whether I have become flawless. I have failed Him, and I still need His mercy. There is room to come honestly, confess what is wrong, and ask for help. Jesus invites the weary to come, and He promises to receive those who come to Him.</p><p>But I must take care when I begin defending the very thing He is asking me to surrender. I can become practiced at explaining why His correction should wait. My words may express love while my choices keep Him at a distance.</p><p>He loves me too much for me to treat that lightly.</p><p>Whether I meet Him through death or live to be changed at His coming, I will stand before the One who already knows me. His story has reached me. His invitation has been offered. My life is answering.</p><p>If I refuse the love of the One who gives me life, where am I choosing to stand?</p><p>I do not want to arrive at the end with a lifetime of explanations for why I would not come.</p><p>He is here now. I can turn toward Him now.</p><p>\u201cLord, I believe You love me. Help me answer You honestly. Show me what I am holding back, and help me entrust it to You.\u201d</p><section aria-labelledby=\"scripture-references\"><h2 id=\"scripture-references\">Scripture references</h2><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew%2023%3A37-39&amp;version=KJV\">Matthew 23:37\u201339</a> \u2014 Jesus\u2019 lament over Jerusalem.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Revelation%202%3A14%3B%202%20Peter%202%3A15-16&amp;version=KJV\">Revelation 2:14; 2 Peter 2:15\u201316</a> \u2014 The warnings concerning Balaam.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Hebrews%204%3A12-16&amp;version=KJV\">Hebrews 4:12\u201316</a> \u2014 Fully known before God and invited to His throne of grace.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew%2011%3A28-30%3B%20John%206%3A37&amp;version=KJV\">Matthew 11:28\u201330; John 6:37</a> \u2014 His invitation and promise to receive those who come.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=2%20Corinthians%205%3A10%3B%201%20Corinthians%2015%3A51-52&amp;version=KJV\">2 Corinthians 5:10; 1 Corinthians 15:51\u201352</a> \u2014 Our accountability and the promised change at His coming.</li></ul></section><nav class=\"reading\" aria-label=\"Return navigation\"><a href=\"/index.html#invitation-title\">Return to the Invitation</a><a href=\"/testimonies#helps\">Writings for the Journey</a></nav></main></body></html>";
