// Approved Sleep Strategy writing, November 11.
PUBLIC_PAGES["/the-sleep-strategy"] = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>The Sleep Strategy \u00b7 Our Shared Journey</title><style>\n:root{color-scheme:light;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;color:#29382f;background:#faf8f2}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0}header,main,footer{max-width:760px;margin:auto;padding:28px 24px}header{border-bottom:1px solid #d9ded4;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;align-items:center}header a{font-size:16px}a{color:#305d45;text-underline-offset:4px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,6vw,46px);font-weight:normal;line-height:1.15;margin:16px 0 24px}h2{font-size:25px;font-weight:normal}p,li{font-size:19px;line-height:1.7}.eyebrow,.notice,footer,.count{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}.eyebrow{letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5a6d5f}.notice{padding:12px 16px;background:#eeeade;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:32px}.placeholder{padding:24px;border:1px dashed #879887;background:#f1f3ec;margin:24px 0;border-radius:5px}.placeholder p{font-size:17px;margin-bottom:0}.media{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}.media .placeholder{margin:0;min-height:145px}nav.reading{margin-top:40px;border-top:1px solid #d9ded4;padding-top:24px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:24px}.next{display:inline-block;padding:13px 19px;background:#305d45;color:white;border-radius:4px;text-decoration:none;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:15px}.menu-list{padding-left:24px}.menu-list li{padding:10px 0}footer{color:#667065;border-top:1px solid #d9ded4;margin-top:32px}.count{color:#667065}a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ab753a;outline-offset:5px}@media(max-width:520px){.media{grid-template-columns:1fr}nav.reading{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}}[hidden]{display:none!important}\n</style><style data-layout=\"centered-reading\">body{display:block}main{margin-inline:auto!important;box-sizing:border-box;min-width:0}main:not(.wrap){width:100%;max-width:760px}main.wrap{width:min(1120px,92%);max-width:1120px}body>header,body>footer{margin-inline:auto;box-sizing:border-box}main h1{text-align:center}main>.eyebrow{display:block;text-align:center}main>.article-subtitle{text-align:center}nav.reading{flex-wrap:wrap}img{max-width:100%}@media(max-width:520px){header{flex-wrap:wrap}main:not(.wrap){padding-inline:22px}main.wrap{width:92%}}</style><link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://speakihear.org/the-sleep-strategy\"></head><body><header><span>Speak I Hear &middot; His Love Story</span><nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"/index.html\">Main Menu</a> &middot; <a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Shared Journey</a></nav></header><main><span class=\"eyebrow\">Our Shared Journey</span><h1>The Sleep Strategy</h1><p><em>The final surrender of the day</em></p>\n<p>For years, I have spoken with God at night just before going to sleep.</p>\n<p>Over the years, things have grown out of that relationship until I began calling what I do my Sleep Strategy.</p>\n<p>This is deeply personal. Yet I am willing to share it if it might help someone who is having difficulty sleeping, falling asleep, or finding peace.</p>\n<p>When I feel that I am approaching sleep, I speak aloud. In Jesus\u2019 name, I tell the enemy and every evil influence to leave. Then I trust the power of Jesus and consider the matter settled.</p>\n<p>\u201cSubmit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.\u201d (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=James+4%3A7&amp;version=ESV\">James 4:7</a>)</p>\n<p>With my Father, I can speak aloud or pray silently. He knows my thoughts before I have formed the words. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm+139%3A1-4&amp;version=ESV\">Psalm 139:1\u20134</a>)</p>\n<p>There are some very dreamy moments as I approach sleep.</p>\n<p>For nearly sixty years, I lost consciousness following whatever strange thought happened to be passing through my mind. A green elephant with pink polka dots, perhaps, or some other unlikely thing. That would be my last thought, and then I would be asleep.</p>\n<p>For the past few years, I have approached that moment differently.</p>\n<p>In my bed, I deliberately turn my thoughts toward Christ. Paul writes about taking every thought captive to obey Him. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=2+Corinthians+10%3A5&amp;version=ESV\">2 Corinthians 10:5</a>)</p>\n<p>That might sound exhausting.</p>\n<p>What I do is simple. When I feel that I am about to lose consciousness, I surrender my consciousness to Him.</p>\n<p>While I am awake, I have a choice about what I do with my attention. I can turn my thoughts toward Him. Then, as sleep comes, I surrender that very awareness.</p>\n<p><strong>My final conscious choice is to give myself to Him.</strong></p>\n<p>Once I am asleep, I am no longer consciously directing my thoughts or making another decision about what I have surrendered. I have entrusted myself to Him as I pass into those hours.</p>\n<p>That is what I mean by the final surrender.</p>\n<p>We spend roughly a third of our lives asleep. Through these years of relationship, I have come to bring that part of my life to Him deliberately.</p>\n<p>The Prince of Peace is with us through the night. He can calm our spirit and give us rest. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Isaiah+9%3A6&amp;version=ESV\">Isaiah 9:6</a>)</p>\n<p>Jesus invites the weary and burdened to come to Him: \u201cI will give you rest.\u201d (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+11%3A28-30&amp;version=ESV\">Matthew 11:28\u201330</a>)</p>\n<p>The One to whom I surrender neither slumbers nor sleeps. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm+121%3A3-4&amp;version=ESV\">Psalm 121:3\u20134</a>)</p>\n<p>This began with speaking to Him at night. Over the years, it grew into something I could scarcely have explained when I began: a relationship in which I have learned to entrust Him with the moment my own awareness slips away.</p>\n<p>David wrote, \u201cIn peace I will both lie down and sleep.\u201d (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm+4%3A8&amp;version=ESV\">Psalm 4:8</a>)</p>\n<p>As I approach sleep, I surrender my consciousness to Him.</p>\n<p><strong>The final surrender of the day.</strong></p><nav class=\"reading\" aria-label=\"Reading navigation\"><a href=\"/take-heart-he-has-overcome\">Previous: Take Heart - He Has Overcome</a><a href=\"/testimonies#helps\">Writings for the Journey</a><a href=\"/index.html\">Main Menu</a></nav></main></body></html>";
