PUBLIC_PAGES["/writings/the-love-that-carries-him.html"] = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>The Love That Carries Him \u00b7 The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"The Love That Carries Him \u2014 a reflection on the love with which Christ continues.\"><style>\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-padding-top:24px}body{margin:0;background:#f7f3ec;color:#302b28;font:20px/1.8 Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif}main,header,footer{width:min(680px,calc(100% - 40px));margin:auto}header{padding:25px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dcd2c4;font:15px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif}a{color:#76522e;text-underline-offset:4px}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #85613a;outline-offset:4px}.title{padding:38px 0 24px}h1{font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(37px,7vw,55px);line-height:1.15;margin:18px 0}h2{font-weight:400;font-size:30px;line-height:1.3;margin:2.2em 0 .8em}p{margin:0 0 1.15em}small,.meta,summary,footer{font:14px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#6b6258}img{display:block;width:min(100%,440px);height:auto;margin:25px auto}.subtitle{font-style:italic;font-size:24px}details{border-block:1px solid #dcd2c4;padding:15px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;color:#76522e}li{margin:8px 0;font-size:17px}footer{padding:30px 0;margin-top:45px;border-top:1px solid #dcd2c4}@media(max-width:400px){body{font-size:19px}}@media print{details,header,.download,footer{display:none}body{background:white;color:black;font-size:12pt}main{width:100%}}\n.end{margin-top:45px;padding-top:25px;border-top:1px solid #dcd2c4}nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px}.skip{position:absolute;top:-100px;background:white;padding:10px}.skip:focus{top:10px}</style><style data-layout=\"centered-reading\">body{display:block}main{margin-inline:auto!important;box-sizing:border-box;min-width:0}main:not(.wrap){width:100%;max-width:760px}main.wrap{width:min(1120px,92%);max-width:1120px}body>header,body>footer{margin-inline:auto;box-sizing:border-box}main h1{text-align:center}main>.eyebrow{display:block;text-align:center}main>.article-subtitle{text-align:center}nav.reading{flex-wrap:wrap}img{max-width:100%}@media(max-width:520px){header{flex-wrap:wrap}main:not(.wrap){padding-inline:22px}main.wrap{width:92%}}</style><link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://speakihear.org/writings/the-love-that-carries-him.html\"></head><body><a class=\"skip\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a><header><nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"../index.html\">\u2190 Home</a><a href=\"scripture-references.html#the-love-that-carries-him\">Scripture references</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"../index.html#story-thread\">Follow the story</a><a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Common Journey</a></nav></header><main id=\"main\"><div class=\"title\"><p class=\"revision\" data-revision=\"A\" style=\"font:12px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#6b6258\">Revision A \u00b7 November 12, 2026</p><p class=\"meta\">THE GREATEST LOVE STORY EVER TOLD</p></div><article><h1>The Love That Carries Him</h1>\n<p><em>The heart of the Lamb</em></p>\n<p>Before we follow Him further, let us consider the scroll we have carried through this story. Upon one side, we have watched the lives of people unfold within the world we know. Upon the other, we have sought glimpses of the eternal purpose that holds those lives within its reach. Yet perhaps we have imagined the two sides too separately, as though turning the scroll could take us somewhere Christ Himself was not already present.</p>\n<p>Picture the scroll itself as the skin of the Lamb. Within this image, He bears both accounts upon Himself: the lives that pass through time and the love that knew them before their days began. The thickness between the two surfaces becomes our picture of the chasm between the physical and the spiritual. To us, that distance exceeds all our ability to cross it. Yet the two sides are held together in Him.</p>\n<p>Here is our Ketubah, the marriage covenant we have been learning to see within the story. The Lamb gives Himself to bring His bride near. We cannot turn a page of this covenant without drawing close to Him, for He is the very substance upon which we have imagined it written.</p>\n<p>Now consider who has come within our reach.</p>\n<p>Jesus is God in the flesh. The Word through whom creation came into being has entered the life of His creatures. He has lived within a human frame, spoken with a human voice, and allowed people to draw near enough to touch Him. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+1%3A1-3%2C14&amp;version=ESV\">John 1:1\u20133, 14</a>) How can we begin to comprehend the wonder of the great I AM walking among us? We have seen Him weary beside a well and asleep upon a boat, while the fullness of deity dwells bodily in Him. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Colossians+2%3A9&amp;version=ESV\">Colossians 2:9</a>)</p>\n<p>Perhaps our familiarity with the account has allowed us to pass too quickly over its immensity. Every ordinary encounter has held a miracle beyond our understanding. Someone has looked into His face, asked Him a question, or received bread from His hands without comprehending the fullness of the One before them.</p>\n<p>And what has He felt as He looked upon them?</p>\n<p>We have watched His compassion move Him toward the weary, the hungry, the grieving, and the lost. He has seen people harassed and helpless, like sheep without a shepherd. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+9%3A36&amp;version=ESV\">Matthew 9:36</a>) He knows the Father whose love they have misunderstood. He knows the care behind the voice they have learned to fear, the welcome beyond the distance they believe cannot be crossed. When the enemy confuses that love, Christ sees the very people He desires to gather drawing away from the One who longs to receive them.</p>\n<p>We hear something of that ache when He speaks over Jerusalem. He has desired to gather her children, yet they have been unwilling. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+23%3A37&amp;version=ESV\">Matthew 23:37</a>) Love stands within their hearing and calls to them. His desire reaches toward theirs, seeking the willing turning of a heart.</p>\n<p>That is the compassion we must carry with us into the hours ahead. His suffering belongs within a purpose whose beginning lies beyond the beginning of our world. He has come knowing what the Father desires, and the Father\u2019s desire is precious to Him. Jesus tells us that He does what He sees the Father doing and speaks as the Father has taught Him. He declares that His obedience will show the world His love for the Father. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+5%3A19%3B8%3A28%3B14%3A31&amp;version=ESV\">John 5:19; 8:28; 14:31</a>)</p>\n<p>Here is the love that carries Him: the love of the Son for the Father, and within their purpose, the compassion that reaches for us. We cannot measure it by the brief span of the road before Him. He walks toward an eternal outcome, toward the gathering of those He desires to have with Him.</p>\n<p>Feel, within our image, the skin of the scroll drawn taut between the two accounts. Upon one surface lie the fears, refusals, and sorrows of our natural lives. Upon the other is the purpose of God, reaching toward the fellowship for which He made us. At the places where the story draws those realities close, imagine the covenant taking on the resonance of a living instrument. The tension gives a sound, and through that sound we begin to hear the heart of Christ.</p>\n<p>We have heard it beside a grave, where He wept. We have heard it in the welcome He gave to people others would have sent away. Soon we shall hear it in the garden, where He brings His anguish before the Father and willingly yields Himself to the Father\u2019s will. The sound belongs to a love that feels the cost and continues toward the beloved.</p>\n<p>Then let our imagination return to the first Adam. God caused a deep sleep to fall upon him, and from his side formed the woman He brought to him. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis+2%3A21-23&amp;version=ESV\">Genesis 2:21\u201323</a>) Carry that image gently toward the Last Adam, and consider His approaching death as the deep sleep from which He will rise to receive His bride. Paul draws marriage itself into this mystery of Christ and the church, speaking of the Lord who loved her and gave Himself for her. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Ephesians+5%3A25-32&amp;version=ESV\">Ephesians 5:25\u201332</a>)</p>\n<p>What would it mean to hear His heart here? Beneath the account of what people will do to Him is the love with which He gives Himself. We may attend so closely to the wounds that we scarcely consider the desire carrying Him through them. He has come to bring her near. Beyond the sorrow before Him lies the joy for which He endures the Cross. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Hebrews+12%3A2&amp;version=ESV\">Hebrews 12:2</a>)</p>\n<p>And we are being invited into that love today. When our desire turns toward Him, when we surrender our will to His, the eternal purpose begins finding expression within our natural lives. These bodies, these words, these ordinary encounters become places where the love of the living Christ may be made known. He has given us the example to follow, and He lives to form His likeness within us.</p>\n<p>John tells us that we are God\u2019s children now, and that we shall be like Christ when we see Him as He is. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1+John+3%3A2-3&amp;version=ESV\">1 John 3:2\u20133</a>) I want to begin yielding to that likeness here. I want the love that moved Him toward the Father\u2019s will and toward our need to become visible in the life I am living.</p>\n<p>So remain with Him before we take another step. Hold the two sides of the scroll together in your thoughts, and remember whose life bears them both. The One who came among us knows the distance we cannot cross. He feels the longing we cannot measure. He sees the bride He desires to bring home, and He offers Himself toward that joy.</p>\n<p>As the covenant draws taut, listen for His heart. The love we are trying to hear is carrying Him into everything He is about to give.</p></article><aside aria-labelledby=\"next-act-title\" style=\"margin:36px 0;padding:24px;border:1px solid #dcd2c4;background:#eee8dc\"><h2 id=\"next-act-title\" style=\"margin:0 0 12px\">The next act</h2><p style=\"margin:0\">I am prayerfully considering the next act of this story. Thank you for walking with me.</p></aside><div class=\"end\"><a href=\"love-goes-to-bring-them-home.html\">\u2190 Love Goes to Bring Them Home</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"scripture-references.html#the-love-that-carries-him\">Scripture references</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"../index.html#story-thread\">Follow the story</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"#main\">Back to top \u2191</a></div><p style=\"margin-top:32px;padding-top:20px;border-top:1px solid #dcd2c4\"><a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Common Journey \u2014 shared memories of His love \u2192</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/index.html\">Main Menu</a></p></main><footer>The Greatest Love Story Ever Told<p></p></footer></body></html>";
PUBLIC_PAGES["/index.html"] = "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>The Heartbeat of Heaven \u00b7 The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Christ-centered writings exploring the love of God: The Greatest Love Story Ever Told, The Invitation, and The Heartbeat of Heaven.\">\n<style>\n:root{--paper:#f7f3ec;--ink:#302b28;--muted:#6b6258;--gold:#85613a;--line:#dcd2c4}*{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-behavior:smooth;scroll-padding-top:24px}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;line-height:1.7}a{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:5px}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--gold);outline-offset:6px}.wrap{width:min(1120px,90%);margin:auto}header{padding:24px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}header .wrap{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:22px;align-items:center}.brand{font-size:18px;text-decoration:none}nav{display:flex;gap:28px;font:13px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}nav a{text-decoration:none}nav a:hover{text-decoration:underline}.eyebrow{font:11px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold)}.intro{text-align:center;padding:57px 0 32px}h1,h2{font-weight:400;line-height:1.12;margin:16px 0}h1{font-size:clamp(39px,5.5vw,66px);max-width:790px;margin:15px auto 22px;letter-spacing:-.035em}.lede{max-width:620px;margin:0 auto;color:var(--muted);font-size:18px}.hero{margin:10px 0 0}.hero img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.hero figcaption{font:11px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;text-align:right;color:var(--muted);padding-top:9px}blockquote{margin:0;text-align:center;padding:48px 15px 55px;font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,31px);line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}blockquote span{display:block}.writing{padding:65px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.45fr;gap:80px}.writing h2{font-size:42px;letter-spacing:-.025em}.writing p{margin:0 0 20px;font-size:18px;color:var(--muted)}.number{font:12px system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:18px}.small{font:12px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--muted)}details{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:14px}summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--gold);font-size:16px}details p{padding-top:18px}.heartbeat{border-block:1px solid var(--line);display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:65px;align-items:center;padding:65px 0}.heartbeat img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.heartbeat h2{font-size:42px;letter-spacing:-.025em}.heartbeat p{font-size:18px;color:var(--muted)}.closing{text-align:center;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:45px 20px}.closing p{margin:8px auto;max-width:620px}.blessing{font-style:italic;font-size:25px}footer{background:#eae3d8;padding:20px;text-align:center;font:11px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:650px){header .wrap{flex-direction:column;gap:12px}nav{gap:20px}.intro{padding-top:36px}.writing,.heartbeat{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:23px;padding:40px 0}.writing h2,.heartbeat h2{font-size:35px}.heartbeat img{max-width:440px;margin:auto}blockquote{padding:32px 0}.hero figcaption{text-align:left}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}}\n.begin{display:inline-block;margin:24px 0 8px;padding:12px 24px;background:#76522e;color:white;border-radius:3px;font:15px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;text-decoration:none}.chapter-list{list-style:none;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px}.chapter-list li{padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px}.chapter-list .available{grid-column:1/-1;background:#eee6d9}.chapter-list span{display:block;font:14px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--muted);margin-top:5px}#story-thread{padding:40px 0}#story-thread h2{font-size:38px}@media(max-width:650px){.chapter-list{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:360px){.chapter-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}}.story-title{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,58px);max-width:800px;margin:15px auto 22px}.heartbeat h1{margin:14px 0 22px}#scripture{padding:40px 0 50px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}#scripture h2{font-size:38px}#scripture p{font-size:18px;color:var(--muted)}nav{flex-wrap:wrap}\n.invitation{padding:72px 0 34px}.invitation-copy{max-width:690px;margin:auto;font-size:20px;color:var(--muted)}.invitation-copy p{margin:0 0 22px}.invitation-copy .personal{font-size:25px;color:var(--ink);margin:30px auto 0;max-width:630px}.hero{margin:0 0 54px}.heartbeat{border-top:0}.story{padding:70px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:center}.story h2{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,52px);max-width:690px;margin:16px auto}.story>p{color:var(--muted);font-size:18px}.actions{display:flex;gap:24px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}.actions .begin{margin:12px 0}.story .actions{justify-content:center}.download{font:15px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}.format{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.chapter-directory{text-align:left;margin-top:30px}.chapter-directory #story-thread{padding:20px 0 0}#scripture{text-align:center;border-top:0;padding:60px 0}.personal-note{padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.personal-note .writing{border:0}.personal-note blockquote{border:0}.heartbeat h2{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,52px)}@media(max-width:650px){.invitation{padding-top:42px}.invitation-copy{font-size:18px}.invitation-copy .personal{font-size:23px}.hero{margin-bottom:20px}.story{padding:42px 0}.actions{gap:18px}}\n.foundation{display:block;text-align:center;padding:56px 0 64px;border:0}.foundation h1{max-width:920px;font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,76px)}.foundation-lede{font-size:22px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 auto 30px}.foundation>img{width:100%;max-width:none;display:block}.foundation-copy{max-width:730px;margin:30px auto 0}.foundation-copy p{font-size:19px;line-height:1.75}.foundation .actions{justify-content:center}.story>.hero{margin:0 0 38px}.story>.hero img{width:100%;height:auto}.story>.hero figcaption{font:12px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--muted);text-align:right}#testimonies{padding:52px 20px}#testimonies h2{font-size:40px}.foundation .small{font-size:14px}@media(max-width:650px){.foundation{padding:32px 0 40px}.foundation-copy p{font-size:18px}.foundation h1{font-size:42px}}\n</style>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"The Greatest Love Story Ever Told\"><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://speakihear.org/assets/glset-identity-v3.jpg\"><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\"><style data-layout=\"centered-reading\">body{display:block}main{margin-inline:auto!important;box-sizing:border-box;min-width:0}main:not(.wrap){width:100%;max-width:760px}main.wrap{width:min(1120px,92%);max-width:1120px}body>header,body>footer{margin-inline:auto;box-sizing:border-box}main h1{text-align:center}main>.eyebrow{display:block;text-align:center}main>.article-subtitle{text-align:center}nav.reading{flex-wrap:wrap}img{max-width:100%}@media(max-width:520px){header{flex-wrap:wrap}main:not(.wrap){padding-inline:22px}main.wrap{width:92%}}</style><style data-layout=\"centered-main-text\">main.wrap{text-align:center}main.wrap .actions{justify-content:center}main.wrap .hero figcaption{text-align:center}main.wrap .chapter-list{text-align:center}main.wrap .personal-note div{text-align:center!important}</style><link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://speakihear.org/\"><style>#heartbeat-title{margin-inline:auto;text-align:center}</style><style data-layout=\"grant-poem\">.grant-poem{max-width:660px;margin:48px auto 20px;padding:44px 24px 36px;border-block:1px solid #c9b892;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f4eddc,#fcf9f2 55%,#eee8d9);text-align:center;color:#302b28}.grant-poem .poem-ornament{font-size:22px;color:#85613a;margin-bottom:18px}.grant-poem h3{font:normal clamp(30px,5vw,42px)/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 12px;letter-spacing:-.025em}.grant-poem .poem-byline{font:13px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#765b3e;margin-bottom:30px}.grant-poem .poem-verses p{font:italic clamp(16px,2.8vw,20px)/1.9 Georgia,serif;color:#433d34;margin:0 0 25px}.grant-poem .poem-date{font:12px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#6b6258;margin-top:28px}.grant-poem .poem-end{margin:20px 0 0}@media(max-width:400px){.grant-poem{padding-inline:12px}.grant-poem .poem-verses p{font-size:16px}}</style></head>\n<body id=\"top\">\n<header><div class=\"wrap\"><a class=\"brand\" href=\"#top\">The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</a><nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"#heartbeat\">Heartbeat of Heaven</a><a href=\"#love-story\">The Love Story</a><a href=\"#testimonies\">Our Shared Journey</a><a href=\"#scripture\">Scripture</a></nav></div></header>\n<main class=\"wrap\"><section class=\"heartbeat foundation\" id=\"heartbeat\" aria-labelledby=\"heartbeat-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Begin here \u00b7 A short story</div><h1 id=\"heartbeat-title\">The Heartbeat of Heaven</h1><p class=\"foundation-lede\">Before we follow the whole story, listen to its heartbeat.</p><img src=\"/assets/heartbeat-of-heaven-v2.jpg\" width=\"1672\" height=\"941\" alt=\"A golden heartbeat rises into a radiant cross, with glory shining through the clouds.\"><div class=\"foundation-copy\"><p>At the Cross, the scroll begins to open, and the glory begins to shine through. Here is a place to begin discovering the heart of God, revealed in Jesus Christ.</p><p>This short story is the foundation for what follows. Begin with <em>The Heartbeat of Heaven</em>, then continue into <em>The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</em>. Along the way, <em>Our Shared Journey</em> offers reflections and helps for living in that love.</p><div class=\"actions\"><a class=\"begin\" href=\"/writings/heartbeat-of-heaven.html\">Begin The Heartbeat of Heaven \u2192</a><a class=\"download\" href=\"/writings/heartbeat-of-heaven-rev-r-a.pdf\" download>Download PDF</a></div><p class=\"small\"><a href=\"#love-story\">Then explore The Greatest Love Story Ever Told \u2193</a></p></div></section>\n<section class=\"intro invitation\" aria-labelledby=\"invitation-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">You are welcome here</div><h2 id=\"invitation-title\" style=\"font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,56px)\">An invitation into<br>overwhelming Love</h2><div class=\"invitation-copy\"><p>There is a love so deep, so wide, and so overwhelming that a lifetime can only begin to discover it\u2014the love of God, revealed in Jesus Christ.</p><p>These writings are an invitation to pause, to wonder, and to discover the heart behind that love. Take your time. Come with your questions, your hopes, and your story.</p><p class=\"personal\">It doesn't matter who you are. If you're reading this, this love is for you.</p></div></section>\n<p class=\"reflection-link\" style=\"text-align:center;margin:0 auto 34px;font-style:italic\"><a href=\"/i-would-and-ye-would-not\">I would \u2026 and ye would not</a></p>\n\n\n<section class=\"story\" id=\"love-story\" aria-labelledby=\"story-title\"><figure class=\"hero\"><img src=\"/assets/glset-identity-v3.jpg\" width=\"1696\" height=\"928\" alt=\"The Greatest Love Story Ever Told: an open scroll and a faint empty tomb above a radiant cross, parted veil, and golden heartbeat, with people gathered in shared light.\"><figcaption>The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</figcaption></figure><div class=\"eyebrow\">Continue \u00b7 The unfolding story</div><h2 id=\"story-title\">The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</h2><p>From Separation to Reconciliation</p><p>The heartbeat opens into the larger story: the Creator\u2019s love, our separation, and His work to bring us home. Follow the story through the generations.</p><div class=\"actions\"><a class=\"begin\" href=\"writings/chapter-0.html\">Read Online</a><a class=\"download\" href=\"writings/the-greatest-love-story-current-chapters.zip\" download>Download <span class=\"format\">ZIP \u00b7 Current writings</span></a></div><p class=\"small\">The download contains all current readings in story order.</p><details class=\"chapter-directory\"><summary>Follow the story</summary><span id=\"chapters\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><section id=\"story-thread\" aria-labelledby=\"chapters-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Follow the family through time</div><h2 id=\"chapters-title\">One love story through the generations</h2><ul class=\"chapter-list\"><li class=\"available\"><a href=\"writings/chapter-0.html\">From Separation to Reconciliation</a><span>Begin reading</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/chapter-1.html\">Before the Beginning</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/chapter-2.html\">The First Home</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/chapter-3.html\">Love\u2019s Promise Within a Family</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/chapter-4.html\">Love Carried from Household to Household</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/love-comes-again-to-bethlehem.html\">Love Comes Again to Bethlehem</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/about-his-fathers-business.html\">About His Father\u2019s Business</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/love-goes-to-bring-them-home.html\">Love Goes to Bring Them Home</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/the-love-that-carries-him.html\">The Love That Carries Him</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li class=\"next-act\"><strong>The next act</strong><span>I am prayerfully considering the next act of this story. Thank you for walking with me.</span></li></ul></section></details><details class=\"personal-note\" id=\"word-of-gratitude\"><summary>A Word of Gratitude</summary><div style=\"max-width:690px;margin:24px auto;text-align:left\"><p class=\"small\">An author\u2019s note</p><p>The work of Dr. Michael S. Heiser helped set me on this journey. His writing opened questions I had not known to ask and encouraged me to look again at the larger story unfolding through Scripture, particularly its glimpses of the unseen realm.</p><p>I regard his work as a blessing from the Lord, and I am grateful for what it stirred in me. As we follow this love story into places his scholarship helped me notice, I want to acknowledge that debt with affection and thanks.</p></div></details></section>\n<section id=\"testimonies\" class=\"closing\" aria-labelledby=\"testimonies-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Walk with us \u00b7 Reflections and helps</div><h2 id=\"testimonies-title\">Our Shared Journey</h2><p>What does this love look like in an ordinary day? Explore personal stories, reflections, and Scripture-based helps for growing in relationship with the Living God.</p><p><a href=\"/testimonies\">Continue to Our Shared Journey \u2192</a></p></section><section id=\"scripture\" aria-labelledby=\"scripture-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Read and explore</div><h2 id=\"scripture-title\">Explore Scripture</h2><p>Open the Bible and explore the story for yourself.</p><p><a class=\"begin\" href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Visit Bible Gateway \u2197</a></p><p><a href=\"writings/scripture-references.html\">Scripture references from these writings \u2192</a></p></section>\n<section class=\"grant-poem\" aria-labelledby=\"grant-poem-title\"><div class=\"poem-ornament\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2726</div><h3 id=\"grant-poem-title\">Grace in the Unknown</h3><div class=\"poem-byline\">By Grant Shull</div><div class=\"poem-verses\"><p>I feel as if I\u2019m walking into the unknown,<br>Not a thing to me has shown.<br>Those habits that bind me,<br>They hinder what I could truly be.</p><p>As I stroll I begin to stagger,<br>But to me it does not matter.<br>For if I fall one thing stays clear,<br>An everlasting love draws near.</p><p>A love not a soul can explain,<br>How comforting it is through constant pain.<br>My path may seem to never end,<br>But if I turn and make amends,</p><p>His grace will wash my past away,<br>And lead me to eternal day.</p></div><div class=\"poem-date\">November 10, 2026</div><div class=\"poem-ornament poem-end\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2726</div></section>\n<details class=\"personal-note\"><summary>Why I\u2019m sharing this</summary><section class=\"writing\" id=\"why-im-sharing\" aria-labelledby=\"why-title\"><div><h2 id=\"why-title\">Why I\u2019m sharing this</h2></div><div><p>I hadn\u2019t planned to make this website. It began quite suddenly, with a desire to share something I have found to be true: God loves us, and His love is worth looking into.</p><p>These writings grow out of my own experience, questions, and reading of the Bible. I\u2019m still learning. I don\u2019t have every answer, but I have found something here that has given me hope, and I want to share it.</p><p>I\u2019m not selling anything or asking anything from you. My hope is simply that something you read here will help you\u2014whether it gives you encouragement, helps you consider a question, or leads you to open the Bible for yourself.</p><p>You\u2019re welcome to take your time.</p></div></section><blockquote>The universe exists because of Love.<span>Love does not exist because of the universe.</span></blockquote></details>\n<section class=\"closing\" aria-label=\"Welcome\"><p class=\"blessing\">May God bless you.</p><p>Welcome. Take your time, and may these writings turn your attention toward Christ.</p></section>\n</main>\n<footer>The Greatest Love Story Ever Told \u00b7 Christ-centered writings<p><a href=\"mailto:sam.thomas@speakihear.org\">Contact a fellow traveller</a></p><p>Shared by a fellow traveller learning to walk with God. Your thoughts and questions are welcome.</p></footer>\n</body></html>\n";

// Approved story finale, replacing next-act notices.
PUBLIC_PAGES["/writings/love-opens-the-way.html"] = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>Love Opens the Way \u00b7 The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"Love Opens the Way \u2014 a reflection on the love with which Christ continues.\"><style>\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-padding-top:24px}body{margin:0;background:#f7f3ec;color:#302b28;font:20px/1.8 Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif}main,header,footer{width:min(680px,calc(100% - 40px));margin:auto}header{padding:25px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dcd2c4;font:15px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif}a{color:#76522e;text-underline-offset:4px}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #85613a;outline-offset:4px}.title{padding:38px 0 24px}h1{font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(37px,7vw,55px);line-height:1.15;margin:18px 0}h2{font-weight:400;font-size:30px;line-height:1.3;margin:2.2em 0 .8em}p{margin:0 0 1.15em}small,.meta,summary,footer{font:14px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#6b6258}img{display:block;width:min(100%,440px);height:auto;margin:25px auto}.subtitle{font-style:italic;font-size:24px}details{border-block:1px solid #dcd2c4;padding:15px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;color:#76522e}li{margin:8px 0;font-size:17px}footer{padding:30px 0;margin-top:45px;border-top:1px solid #dcd2c4}@media(max-width:400px){body{font-size:19px}}@media print{details,header,.download,footer{display:none}body{background:white;color:black;font-size:12pt}main{width:100%}}\n.end{margin-top:45px;padding-top:25px;border-top:1px solid #dcd2c4}nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px}.skip{position:absolute;top:-100px;background:white;padding:10px}.skip:focus{top:10px}</style><style data-layout=\"centered-reading\">body{display:block}main{margin-inline:auto!important;box-sizing:border-box;min-width:0}main:not(.wrap){width:100%;max-width:760px}main.wrap{width:min(1120px,92%);max-width:1120px}body>header,body>footer{margin-inline:auto;box-sizing:border-box}main h1{text-align:center}main>.eyebrow{display:block;text-align:center}main>.article-subtitle{text-align:center}nav.reading{flex-wrap:wrap}img{max-width:100%}@media(max-width:520px){header{flex-wrap:wrap}main:not(.wrap){padding-inline:22px}main.wrap{width:92%}}</style><link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://speakihear.org/writings/love-opens-the-way.html\"></head><body><a class=\"skip\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a><header><nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"../index.html\">\u2190 Home</a><a href=\"scripture-references.html#the-love-that-carries-him\">Scripture references</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"../index.html#story-thread\">Follow the story</a><a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Common Journey</a></nav></header><main id=\"main\"><div class=\"title\"><p class=\"revision\" data-revision=\"1\" style=\"font:12px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#6b6258\">Revision 1 \u00b7 November 12, 2026</p><p class=\"meta\">THE GREATEST LOVE STORY EVER TOLD \u00b7 FINAL CHAPTER</p></div><article><h1>Love Opens the Way</h1>\n<p><em>The other side of the scroll</em></p>\n<p>The love that carries Him has brought us here. He knows what the Father desires, and He has come willingly to accomplish it. Within that love is the bride He longs to bring near, the people whose lives we have followed through the generations, and those still to come. He holds their history and their hope together in Himself.</p>\n<p>Remember the scroll we have been carrying. In our telling, its substance is the skin of the Lamb, the Ketubah upon which we imagine the covenant written. One surface bears the unfolding of our natural lives; the other carries the eternal purpose we have been trying to glimpse. Christ knows both sides. He exists upon both sides at once, holding together what we cannot bring together ourselves.</p>\n<p>Now imagine His blood touching that covenant.</p>\n<p>The crimson enters the surface and spreads through the skin. What appears upon one side reaches the other, until the same stain belongs to both. Within this image, the distance we have pictured between the physical and the spiritual is crossed by the offering of the One who bears them. His blood saturates the very substance holding the two accounts together.</p>\n<p>We can remain here without following every wound. The love with which He gives Himself is already beyond our ability to measure. Through His blood, Scripture tells us, those once far away are brought near. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Ephesians+2%3A13&amp;version=ESV\">Ephesians 2:13</a>) Across our imagined scroll, the crimson becomes the visible expression of that nearness. The covenant bears upon both sides the cost He has willingly paid.</p>\n<p>What must this mean to the forces aligned against Him?</p>\n<p>For generations, human history has carried the consequences of separation from God. Into that history came Jesus, commanding unclean spirits, restoring broken lives, and calling people into the love of the Father. His presence disturbed what had seemed so firmly established. Even death yielded when He called a man from his tomb.</p>\n<p>Then they saw Him die.</p>\n<p>Consider the terrible mistake concealed within that apparent victory. They had brought about the death of the man without comprehending the purpose of the One who had entered humanity. Paul tells us that the rulers of this age did not understand God\u2019s hidden wisdom; had they understood, they would not have crucified the Lord of glory. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1+Corinthians+2%3A7-8&amp;version=ESV\">1 Corinthians 2:7\u20138</a>)</p>\n<p>From the other side of the scroll, we begin to consider what their victory had actually accomplished. The death they had helped bring about belonged within the purpose God had held before the ages. The One they opposed had willingly entered the condition through which He would break their hold. Hebrews describes Christ overcoming the one who held the power of death through death itself, bringing release to those enslaved by its fear. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Hebrews+2%3A14-15&amp;version=ESV\">Hebrews 2:14\u201315</a>)</p>\n<p>They had made a grave error in the execution of the man. The man was the Lord of glory, and His surrender had carried Him into the very place from which humanity needed deliverance.</p>\n<p>Let that discovery have its weight. We need no imagined weapons or spectacle to make His authority immense. We have already seen a little of what happens when He identifies Himself: those who came to arrest Him drew back and fell to the ground. He then gave Himself into their hands. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+18%3A4-12&amp;version=ESV\">John 18:4\u201312</a>) What they were permitted to do proceeded within His willingness to fulfill the Father\u2019s purpose.</p>\n<p>Now Paul speaks of rulers and authorities disarmed, exposed, and triumphed over through the Cross. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Colossians+2%3A13-15&amp;version=ESV\">Colossians 2:13\u201315</a>) What had appeared to be the removal of the One troubling them had become the disclosure of a purpose they had failed to comprehend. The covenant was receiving His blood, and the two sides of our scroll were being drawn together through His offering.</p>\n<p>Then come those three days, over which I can only pause in wonder. I do not know everything taking place beyond the sight of those who mourned Him. Peter gives us the account of Christ\u2019s proclamation to spirits in prison, and I find myself considering how much those few words hold. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1+Peter+3%3A18-20&amp;version=ESV\">1 Peter 3:18\u201320</a>) The people could know where His body had been laid. They could not stand outside that tomb and comprehend the reach of His work.</p>\n<p>We can allow the unknown to remain vast. The risen Lord tells us that He lives forevermore and holds the keys of Death and Hades. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Revelation+1%3A17-18&amp;version=ESV\">Revelation 1:17\u201318</a>) Those words give us something to carry through the silence: the authority belongs to Him, and the One who entered death will emerge beyond its dominion.</p>\n<p>Here I find another image forming. The Master has the keys, and He is making copies for His followers. That is how I picture the generosity of what He has accomplished\u2014the way He opens access and brings others into the life He possesses. Jesus speaks of giving the keys of the Kingdom, and Hebrews invites us to enter God\u2019s presence through the new and living way opened by His blood. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+16%3A19&amp;version=ESV\">Matthew 16:19</a>; <a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Hebrews+10%3A19-22&amp;version=ESV\">Hebrews 10:19\u201322</a>) The victory reaches toward the very people He came to gather.</p>\n<p>Return now to the deep sleep of the first Adam. From his side, God formed the woman He brought to him. We have carried that image toward the Last Adam, considering His death as the deep sleep through which He gives Himself for His bride. Paul speaks of Christ loving the church and giving Himself for her, drawing marriage into the mystery of their belonging. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis+2%3A21-23&amp;version=ESV\">Genesis 2:21\u201323</a>; <a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Ephesians+5%3A25-32&amp;version=ESV\">Ephesians 5:25\u201332</a>)</p>\n<p>The love that brought Him here has reached beyond what His followers could see. While they grieve the loss of His presence, the purpose of bringing them near is being fulfilled. Their sorrow is real, but it cannot yet tell them what their Lord has accomplished.</p>\n<p>Morning comes, and we find ourselves in a garden again. Our story began in a garden, with humanity receiving life from God and then turning away. Here, beside another garden tomb, the Last Adam is alive. Paul calls Him a life-giving spirit and directs our hope toward bearing His heavenly likeness. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1+Corinthians+15%3A45-49&amp;version=ESV\">1 Corinthians 15:45\u201349</a>) The life before us reaches beyond the mortal existence we have known.</p>\n<p>Mary stands weeping until He speaks her name. In that recognition, the immensity of His work becomes intimate enough for one person to receive. He knows her, and she knows Him. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+20%3A11-16&amp;version=ESV\">John 20:11\u201316</a>) The Lord who has passed through death has come within her hearing, and His voice carries the relationship through what she believed had ended it.</p>\n<p>Hold the scroll close once more. The crimson has reached both surfaces, and the same Christ holds them together. What was offered within human history opens into eternal life; what God purposed beyond our sight now invites us into fellowship with Him. We can begin surrendering ourselves to that love today, allowing the life of the risen Christ to find expression in the bodies, words, and actions through which we live.</p>\n<p>He has given Himself to bring His bride near. As we walk with Him into the garden, we are only beginning to discover what His love has opened.</p></article><div class=\"end\"><a href=\"the-love-that-carries-him.html\">\u2190 The Love That Carries Him</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/index.html#story-thread\">Follow the story</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"#main\">Back to top \u2191</a></div><p style=\"margin-top:32px;padding-top:20px;border-top:1px solid #dcd2c4\"><a href=\"/testimonies\">Continue exploring Our Shared Journey \u2192</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/index.html\">Main Menu</a></p></main><footer>The Greatest Love Story Ever Told<p></p></footer></body></html>";
PUBLIC_PAGES["/writings/the-love-that-carries-him.html"] = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>The Love That Carries Him \u00b7 The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"The Love That Carries Him \u2014 a reflection on the love with which Christ continues.\"><style>\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-padding-top:24px}body{margin:0;background:#f7f3ec;color:#302b28;font:20px/1.8 Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif}main,header,footer{width:min(680px,calc(100% - 40px));margin:auto}header{padding:25px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #dcd2c4;font:15px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif}a{color:#76522e;text-underline-offset:4px}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #85613a;outline-offset:4px}.title{padding:38px 0 24px}h1{font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(37px,7vw,55px);line-height:1.15;margin:18px 0}h2{font-weight:400;font-size:30px;line-height:1.3;margin:2.2em 0 .8em}p{margin:0 0 1.15em}small,.meta,summary,footer{font:14px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#6b6258}img{display:block;width:min(100%,440px);height:auto;margin:25px auto}.subtitle{font-style:italic;font-size:24px}details{border-block:1px solid #dcd2c4;padding:15px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;color:#76522e}li{margin:8px 0;font-size:17px}footer{padding:30px 0;margin-top:45px;border-top:1px solid #dcd2c4}@media(max-width:400px){body{font-size:19px}}@media print{details,header,.download,footer{display:none}body{background:white;color:black;font-size:12pt}main{width:100%}}\n.end{margin-top:45px;padding-top:25px;border-top:1px solid #dcd2c4}nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px}.skip{position:absolute;top:-100px;background:white;padding:10px}.skip:focus{top:10px}</style><style data-layout=\"centered-reading\">body{display:block}main{margin-inline:auto!important;box-sizing:border-box;min-width:0}main:not(.wrap){width:100%;max-width:760px}main.wrap{width:min(1120px,92%);max-width:1120px}body>header,body>footer{margin-inline:auto;box-sizing:border-box}main h1{text-align:center}main>.eyebrow{display:block;text-align:center}main>.article-subtitle{text-align:center}nav.reading{flex-wrap:wrap}img{max-width:100%}@media(max-width:520px){header{flex-wrap:wrap}main:not(.wrap){padding-inline:22px}main.wrap{width:92%}}</style><link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://speakihear.org/writings/the-love-that-carries-him.html\"></head><body><a class=\"skip\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a><header><nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"../index.html\">\u2190 Home</a><a href=\"scripture-references.html#the-love-that-carries-him\">Scripture references</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"../index.html#story-thread\">Follow the story</a><a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Common Journey</a></nav></header><main id=\"main\"><div class=\"title\"><p class=\"revision\" data-revision=\"A\" style=\"font:12px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#6b6258\">Revision A \u00b7 November 12, 2026</p><p class=\"meta\">THE GREATEST LOVE STORY EVER TOLD</p></div><article><h1>The Love That Carries Him</h1>\n<p><em>The heart of the Lamb</em></p>\n<p>Before we follow Him further, let us consider the scroll we have carried through this story. Upon one side, we have watched the lives of people unfold within the world we know. Upon the other, we have sought glimpses of the eternal purpose that holds those lives within its reach. Yet perhaps we have imagined the two sides too separately, as though turning the scroll could take us somewhere Christ Himself was not already present.</p>\n<p>Picture the scroll itself as the skin of the Lamb. Within this image, He bears both accounts upon Himself: the lives that pass through time and the love that knew them before their days began. The thickness between the two surfaces becomes our picture of the chasm between the physical and the spiritual. To us, that distance exceeds all our ability to cross it. Yet the two sides are held together in Him.</p>\n<p>Here is our Ketubah, the marriage covenant we have been learning to see within the story. The Lamb gives Himself to bring His bride near. We cannot turn a page of this covenant without drawing close to Him, for He is the very substance upon which we have imagined it written.</p>\n<p>Now consider who has come within our reach.</p>\n<p>Jesus is God in the flesh. The Word through whom creation came into being has entered the life of His creatures. He has lived within a human frame, spoken with a human voice, and allowed people to draw near enough to touch Him. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+1%3A1-3%2C14&amp;version=ESV\">John 1:1\u20133, 14</a>) How can we begin to comprehend the wonder of the great I AM walking among us? We have seen Him weary beside a well and asleep upon a boat, while the fullness of deity dwells bodily in Him. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Colossians+2%3A9&amp;version=ESV\">Colossians 2:9</a>)</p>\n<p>Perhaps our familiarity with the account has allowed us to pass too quickly over its immensity. Every ordinary encounter has held a miracle beyond our understanding. Someone has looked into His face, asked Him a question, or received bread from His hands without comprehending the fullness of the One before them.</p>\n<p>And what has He felt as He looked upon them?</p>\n<p>We have watched His compassion move Him toward the weary, the hungry, the grieving, and the lost. He has seen people harassed and helpless, like sheep without a shepherd. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+9%3A36&amp;version=ESV\">Matthew 9:36</a>) He knows the Father whose love they have misunderstood. He knows the care behind the voice they have learned to fear, the welcome beyond the distance they believe cannot be crossed. When the enemy confuses that love, Christ sees the very people He desires to gather drawing away from the One who longs to receive them.</p>\n<p>We hear something of that ache when He speaks over Jerusalem. He has desired to gather her children, yet they have been unwilling. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew+23%3A37&amp;version=ESV\">Matthew 23:37</a>) Love stands within their hearing and calls to them. His desire reaches toward theirs, seeking the willing turning of a heart.</p>\n<p>That is the compassion we must carry with us into the hours ahead. His suffering belongs within a purpose whose beginning lies beyond the beginning of our world. He has come knowing what the Father desires, and the Father\u2019s desire is precious to Him. Jesus tells us that He does what He sees the Father doing and speaks as the Father has taught Him. He declares that His obedience will show the world His love for the Father. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=John+5%3A19%3B8%3A28%3B14%3A31&amp;version=ESV\">John 5:19; 8:28; 14:31</a>)</p>\n<p>Here is the love that carries Him: the love of the Son for the Father, and within their purpose, the compassion that reaches for us. We cannot measure it by the brief span of the road before Him. He walks toward an eternal outcome, toward the gathering of those He desires to have with Him.</p>\n<p>Feel, within our image, the skin of the scroll drawn taut between the two accounts. Upon one surface lie the fears, refusals, and sorrows of our natural lives. Upon the other is the purpose of God, reaching toward the fellowship for which He made us. At the places where the story draws those realities close, imagine the covenant taking on the resonance of a living instrument. The tension gives a sound, and through that sound we begin to hear the heart of Christ.</p>\n<p>We have heard it beside a grave, where He wept. We have heard it in the welcome He gave to people others would have sent away. Soon we shall hear it in the garden, where He brings His anguish before the Father and willingly yields Himself to the Father\u2019s will. The sound belongs to a love that feels the cost and continues toward the beloved.</p>\n<p>Then let our imagination return to the first Adam. God caused a deep sleep to fall upon him, and from his side formed the woman He brought to him. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis+2%3A21-23&amp;version=ESV\">Genesis 2:21\u201323</a>) Carry that image gently toward the Last Adam, and consider His approaching death as the deep sleep from which He will rise to receive His bride. Paul draws marriage itself into this mystery of Christ and the church, speaking of the Lord who loved her and gave Himself for her. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Ephesians+5%3A25-32&amp;version=ESV\">Ephesians 5:25\u201332</a>)</p>\n<p>What would it mean to hear His heart here? Beneath the account of what people will do to Him is the love with which He gives Himself. We may attend so closely to the wounds that we scarcely consider the desire carrying Him through them. He has come to bring her near. Beyond the sorrow before Him lies the joy for which He endures the Cross. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Hebrews+12%3A2&amp;version=ESV\">Hebrews 12:2</a>)</p>\n<p>And we are being invited into that love today. When our desire turns toward Him, when we surrender our will to His, the eternal purpose begins finding expression within our natural lives. These bodies, these words, these ordinary encounters become places where the love of the living Christ may be made known. He has given us the example to follow, and He lives to form His likeness within us.</p>\n<p>John tells us that we are God\u2019s children now, and that we shall be like Christ when we see Him as He is. (<a href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1+John+3%3A2-3&amp;version=ESV\">1 John 3:2\u20133</a>) I want to begin yielding to that likeness here. I want the love that moved Him toward the Father\u2019s will and toward our need to become visible in the life I am living.</p>\n<p>So remain with Him before we take another step. Hold the two sides of the scroll together in your thoughts, and remember whose life bears them both. The One who came among us knows the distance we cannot cross. He feels the longing we cannot measure. He sees the bride He desires to bring home, and He offers Himself toward that joy.</p>\n<p>As the covenant draws taut, listen for His heart. The love we are trying to hear is carrying Him into everything He is about to give.</p></article><nav aria-label=\"Continue the story\" class=\"end\"><a href=\"love-opens-the-way.html\">Continue: Love Opens the Way \u2192</a></nav><div class=\"end\"><a href=\"love-goes-to-bring-them-home.html\">\u2190 Love Goes to Bring Them Home</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"scripture-references.html#the-love-that-carries-him\">Scripture references</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"../index.html#story-thread\">Follow the story</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"#main\">Back to top \u2191</a></div><p style=\"margin-top:32px;padding-top:20px;border-top:1px solid #dcd2c4\"><a href=\"/testimonies\">Our Common Journey \u2014 shared memories of His love \u2192</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/index.html\">Main Menu</a></p></main><footer>The Greatest Love Story Ever Told<p></p></footer></body></html>";
PUBLIC_PAGES["/index.html"] = "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>The Heartbeat of Heaven \u00b7 The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Christ-centered writings exploring the love of God: The Greatest Love Story Ever Told, The Invitation, and The Heartbeat of Heaven.\">\n<style>\n:root{--paper:#f7f3ec;--ink:#302b28;--muted:#6b6258;--gold:#85613a;--line:#dcd2c4}*{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-behavior:smooth;scroll-padding-top:24px}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;line-height:1.7}a{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:5px}a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--gold);outline-offset:6px}.wrap{width:min(1120px,90%);margin:auto}header{padding:24px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}header .wrap{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:22px;align-items:center}.brand{font-size:18px;text-decoration:none}nav{display:flex;gap:28px;font:13px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}nav a{text-decoration:none}nav a:hover{text-decoration:underline}.eyebrow{font:11px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--gold)}.intro{text-align:center;padding:57px 0 32px}h1,h2{font-weight:400;line-height:1.12;margin:16px 0}h1{font-size:clamp(39px,5.5vw,66px);max-width:790px;margin:15px auto 22px;letter-spacing:-.035em}.lede{max-width:620px;margin:0 auto;color:var(--muted);font-size:18px}.hero{margin:10px 0 0}.hero img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.hero figcaption{font:11px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;text-align:right;color:var(--muted);padding-top:9px}blockquote{margin:0;text-align:center;padding:48px 15px 55px;font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,31px);line-height:1.5;font-style:italic;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}blockquote span{display:block}.writing{padding:65px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.45fr;gap:80px}.writing h2{font-size:42px;letter-spacing:-.025em}.writing p{margin:0 0 20px;font-size:18px;color:var(--muted)}.number{font:12px system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:18px}.small{font:12px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--muted)}details{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:14px}summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--gold);font-size:16px}details p{padding-top:18px}.heartbeat{border-block:1px solid var(--line);display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:65px;align-items:center;padding:65px 0}.heartbeat img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.heartbeat h2{font-size:42px;letter-spacing:-.025em}.heartbeat p{font-size:18px;color:var(--muted)}.closing{text-align:center;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:45px 20px}.closing p{margin:8px auto;max-width:620px}.blessing{font-style:italic;font-size:25px}footer{background:#eae3d8;padding:20px;text-align:center;font:11px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:650px){header .wrap{flex-direction:column;gap:12px}nav{gap:20px}.intro{padding-top:36px}.writing,.heartbeat{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:23px;padding:40px 0}.writing h2,.heartbeat h2{font-size:35px}.heartbeat img{max-width:440px;margin:auto}blockquote{padding:32px 0}.hero figcaption{text-align:left}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}}\n.begin{display:inline-block;margin:24px 0 8px;padding:12px 24px;background:#76522e;color:white;border-radius:3px;font:15px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;text-decoration:none}.chapter-list{list-style:none;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px}.chapter-list li{padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px}.chapter-list .available{grid-column:1/-1;background:#eee6d9}.chapter-list span{display:block;font:14px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--muted);margin-top:5px}#story-thread{padding:40px 0}#story-thread h2{font-size:38px}@media(max-width:650px){.chapter-list{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:360px){.chapter-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}}.story-title{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,58px);max-width:800px;margin:15px auto 22px}.heartbeat h1{margin:14px 0 22px}#scripture{padding:40px 0 50px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}#scripture h2{font-size:38px}#scripture p{font-size:18px;color:var(--muted)}nav{flex-wrap:wrap}\n.invitation{padding:72px 0 34px}.invitation-copy{max-width:690px;margin:auto;font-size:20px;color:var(--muted)}.invitation-copy p{margin:0 0 22px}.invitation-copy .personal{font-size:25px;color:var(--ink);margin:30px auto 0;max-width:630px}.hero{margin:0 0 54px}.heartbeat{border-top:0}.story{padding:70px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:center}.story h2{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,52px);max-width:690px;margin:16px auto}.story>p{color:var(--muted);font-size:18px}.actions{display:flex;gap:24px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}.actions .begin{margin:12px 0}.story .actions{justify-content:center}.download{font:15px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}.format{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.chapter-directory{text-align:left;margin-top:30px}.chapter-directory #story-thread{padding:20px 0 0}#scripture{text-align:center;border-top:0;padding:60px 0}.personal-note{padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.personal-note .writing{border:0}.personal-note blockquote{border:0}.heartbeat h2{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,52px)}@media(max-width:650px){.invitation{padding-top:42px}.invitation-copy{font-size:18px}.invitation-copy .personal{font-size:23px}.hero{margin-bottom:20px}.story{padding:42px 0}.actions{gap:18px}}\n.foundation{display:block;text-align:center;padding:56px 0 64px;border:0}.foundation h1{max-width:920px;font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,76px)}.foundation-lede{font-size:22px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 auto 30px}.foundation>img{width:100%;max-width:none;display:block}.foundation-copy{max-width:730px;margin:30px auto 0}.foundation-copy p{font-size:19px;line-height:1.75}.foundation .actions{justify-content:center}.story>.hero{margin:0 0 38px}.story>.hero img{width:100%;height:auto}.story>.hero figcaption{font:12px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--muted);text-align:right}#testimonies{padding:52px 20px}#testimonies h2{font-size:40px}.foundation .small{font-size:14px}@media(max-width:650px){.foundation{padding:32px 0 40px}.foundation-copy p{font-size:18px}.foundation h1{font-size:42px}}\n</style>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"The Greatest Love Story Ever Told\"><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://speakihear.org/assets/glset-identity-v3.jpg\"><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\"><style data-layout=\"centered-reading\">body{display:block}main{margin-inline:auto!important;box-sizing:border-box;min-width:0}main:not(.wrap){width:100%;max-width:760px}main.wrap{width:min(1120px,92%);max-width:1120px}body>header,body>footer{margin-inline:auto;box-sizing:border-box}main h1{text-align:center}main>.eyebrow{display:block;text-align:center}main>.article-subtitle{text-align:center}nav.reading{flex-wrap:wrap}img{max-width:100%}@media(max-width:520px){header{flex-wrap:wrap}main:not(.wrap){padding-inline:22px}main.wrap{width:92%}}</style><style data-layout=\"centered-main-text\">main.wrap{text-align:center}main.wrap .actions{justify-content:center}main.wrap .hero figcaption{text-align:center}main.wrap .chapter-list{text-align:center}main.wrap .personal-note div{text-align:center!important}</style><link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://speakihear.org/\"><style>#heartbeat-title{margin-inline:auto;text-align:center}</style><style data-layout=\"grant-poem\">.grant-poem{max-width:660px;margin:48px auto 20px;padding:44px 24px 36px;border-block:1px solid #c9b892;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f4eddc,#fcf9f2 55%,#eee8d9);text-align:center;color:#302b28}.grant-poem .poem-ornament{font-size:22px;color:#85613a;margin-bottom:18px}.grant-poem h3{font:normal clamp(30px,5vw,42px)/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 12px;letter-spacing:-.025em}.grant-poem .poem-byline{font:13px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#765b3e;margin-bottom:30px}.grant-poem .poem-verses p{font:italic clamp(16px,2.8vw,20px)/1.9 Georgia,serif;color:#433d34;margin:0 0 25px}.grant-poem .poem-date{font:12px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#6b6258;margin-top:28px}.grant-poem .poem-end{margin:20px 0 0}@media(max-width:400px){.grant-poem{padding-inline:12px}.grant-poem .poem-verses p{font-size:16px}}</style></head>\n<body id=\"top\">\n<header><div class=\"wrap\"><a class=\"brand\" href=\"#top\">The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</a><nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"#heartbeat\">Heartbeat of Heaven</a><a href=\"#love-story\">The Love Story</a><a href=\"#testimonies\">Our Shared Journey</a><a href=\"#scripture\">Scripture</a></nav></div></header>\n<main class=\"wrap\"><section class=\"heartbeat foundation\" id=\"heartbeat\" aria-labelledby=\"heartbeat-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Begin here \u00b7 A short story</div><h1 id=\"heartbeat-title\">The Heartbeat of Heaven</h1><p class=\"foundation-lede\">Before we follow the whole story, listen to its heartbeat.</p><img src=\"/assets/heartbeat-of-heaven-v2.jpg\" width=\"1672\" height=\"941\" alt=\"A golden heartbeat rises into a radiant cross, with glory shining through the clouds.\"><div class=\"foundation-copy\"><p>At the Cross, the scroll begins to open, and the glory begins to shine through. Here is a place to begin discovering the heart of God, revealed in Jesus Christ.</p><p>This short story is the foundation for what follows. Begin with <em>The Heartbeat of Heaven</em>, then continue into <em>The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</em>. Along the way, <em>Our Shared Journey</em> offers reflections and helps for living in that love.</p><div class=\"actions\"><a class=\"begin\" href=\"/writings/heartbeat-of-heaven.html\">Begin The Heartbeat of Heaven \u2192</a><a class=\"download\" href=\"/writings/heartbeat-of-heaven-rev-r-a.pdf\" download>Download PDF</a></div><p class=\"small\"><a href=\"#love-story\">Then explore The Greatest Love Story Ever Told \u2193</a></p></div></section>\n<section class=\"intro invitation\" aria-labelledby=\"invitation-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">You are welcome here</div><h2 id=\"invitation-title\" style=\"font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,56px)\">An invitation into<br>overwhelming Love</h2><div class=\"invitation-copy\"><p>There is a love so deep, so wide, and so overwhelming that a lifetime can only begin to discover it\u2014the love of God, revealed in Jesus Christ.</p><p>These writings are an invitation to pause, to wonder, and to discover the heart behind that love. Take your time. Come with your questions, your hopes, and your story.</p><p class=\"personal\">It doesn't matter who you are. If you're reading this, this love is for you.</p></div></section>\n<p class=\"reflection-link\" style=\"text-align:center;margin:0 auto 34px;font-style:italic\"><a href=\"/i-would-and-ye-would-not\">I would \u2026 and ye would not</a></p>\n\n\n<section class=\"story\" id=\"love-story\" aria-labelledby=\"story-title\"><figure class=\"hero\"><img src=\"/assets/glset-identity-v3.jpg\" width=\"1696\" height=\"928\" alt=\"The Greatest Love Story Ever Told: an open scroll and a faint empty tomb above a radiant cross, parted veil, and golden heartbeat, with people gathered in shared light.\"><figcaption>The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</figcaption></figure><div class=\"eyebrow\">Continue \u00b7 The unfolding story</div><h2 id=\"story-title\">The Greatest Love Story Ever Told</h2><p>From Separation to Reconciliation</p><p>The heartbeat opens into the larger story: the Creator\u2019s love, our separation, and His work to bring us home. Follow the story through the generations.</p><div class=\"actions\"><a class=\"begin\" href=\"writings/chapter-0.html\">Read Online</a><a class=\"download\" href=\"writings/the-greatest-love-story-current-chapters.zip\" download>Download <span class=\"format\">ZIP \u00b7 Current writings</span></a></div><p class=\"small\">The download contains all current readings in story order.</p><details class=\"chapter-directory\"><summary>Follow the story</summary><span id=\"chapters\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><section id=\"story-thread\" aria-labelledby=\"chapters-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Follow the family through time</div><h2 id=\"chapters-title\">One love story through the generations</h2><ul class=\"chapter-list\"><li class=\"available\"><a href=\"writings/chapter-0.html\">From Separation to Reconciliation</a><span>Begin reading</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/chapter-1.html\">Before the Beginning</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/chapter-2.html\">The First Home</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/chapter-3.html\">Love\u2019s Promise Within a Family</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/chapter-4.html\">Love Carried from Household to Household</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/love-comes-again-to-bethlehem.html\">Love Comes Again to Bethlehem</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/about-his-fathers-business.html\">About His Father\u2019s Business</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/love-goes-to-bring-them-home.html\">Love Goes to Bring Them Home</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"writings/the-love-that-carries-him.html\">The Love That Carries Him</a><span>Continue the story</span></li><li><a href=\"/writings/love-opens-the-way.html\">Love Opens the Way</a><span>The final chapter</span></li></ul></section></details><details class=\"personal-note\" id=\"word-of-gratitude\"><summary>A Word of Gratitude</summary><div style=\"max-width:690px;margin:24px auto;text-align:left\"><p class=\"small\">An author\u2019s note</p><p>The work of Dr. Michael S. Heiser helped set me on this journey. His writing opened questions I had not known to ask and encouraged me to look again at the larger story unfolding through Scripture, particularly its glimpses of the unseen realm.</p><p>I regard his work as a blessing from the Lord, and I am grateful for what it stirred in me. As we follow this love story into places his scholarship helped me notice, I want to acknowledge that debt with affection and thanks.</p></div></details></section>\n<section id=\"testimonies\" class=\"closing\" aria-labelledby=\"testimonies-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Walk with us \u00b7 Reflections and helps</div><h2 id=\"testimonies-title\">Our Shared Journey</h2><p>What does this love look like in an ordinary day? Explore personal stories, reflections, and Scripture-based helps for growing in relationship with the Living God.</p><p><a href=\"/testimonies\">Continue to Our Shared Journey \u2192</a></p></section><section id=\"scripture\" aria-labelledby=\"scripture-title\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Read and explore</div><h2 id=\"scripture-title\">Explore Scripture</h2><p>Open the Bible and explore the story for yourself.</p><p><a class=\"begin\" href=\"https://www.biblegateway.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Visit Bible Gateway \u2197</a></p><p><a href=\"writings/scripture-references.html\">Scripture references from these writings \u2192</a></p></section>\n<section class=\"grant-poem\" aria-labelledby=\"grant-poem-title\"><div class=\"poem-ornament\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2726</div><h3 id=\"grant-poem-title\">Grace in the Unknown</h3><div class=\"poem-byline\">By Grant Shull</div><div class=\"poem-verses\"><p>I feel as if I\u2019m walking into the unknown,<br>Not a thing to me has shown.<br>Those habits that bind me,<br>They hinder what I could truly be.</p><p>As I stroll I begin to stagger,<br>But to me it does not matter.<br>For if I fall one thing stays clear,<br>An everlasting love draws near.</p><p>A love not a soul can explain,<br>How comforting it is through constant pain.<br>My path may seem to never end,<br>But if I turn and make amends,</p><p>His grace will wash my past away,<br>And lead me to eternal day.</p></div><div class=\"poem-date\">November 10, 2026</div><div class=\"poem-ornament poem-end\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u2726</div></section>\n<details class=\"personal-note\"><summary>Why I\u2019m sharing this</summary><section class=\"writing\" id=\"why-im-sharing\" aria-labelledby=\"why-title\"><div><h2 id=\"why-title\">Why I\u2019m sharing this</h2></div><div><p>I hadn\u2019t planned to make this website. It began quite suddenly, with a desire to share something I have found to be true: God loves us, and His love is worth looking into.</p><p>These writings grow out of my own experience, questions, and reading of the Bible. I\u2019m still learning. I don\u2019t have every answer, but I have found something here that has given me hope, and I want to share it.</p><p>I\u2019m not selling anything or asking anything from you. My hope is simply that something you read here will help you\u2014whether it gives you encouragement, helps you consider a question, or leads you to open the Bible for yourself.</p><p>You\u2019re welcome to take your time.</p></div></section><blockquote>The universe exists because of Love.<span>Love does not exist because of the universe.</span></blockquote></details>\n<section class=\"closing\" aria-label=\"Welcome\"><p class=\"blessing\">May God bless you.</p><p>Welcome. Take your time, and may these writings turn your attention toward Christ.</p></section>\n</main>\n<footer>The Greatest Love Story Ever Told \u00b7 Christ-centered writings<p><a href=\"mailto:sam.thomas@speakihear.org\">Contact a fellow traveller</a></p><p>Shared by a fellow traveller learning to walk with God. Your thoughts and questions are welcome.</p></footer>\n</body></html>\n";

